window.MODULES=[{"t":"Selenium Introduction","s":"What Selenium is, its components, and how it compares with other tools.","est":"25 min","lvl":"Beginner","an":["<b>The story used in every module:</b> <b>Selly</b>, a robot courier, delivers parcels inside <b>Selenium Mall</b>. The mall is your <b>website</b>, each shop is a <b>web element</b>, and Selly is <b>Selenium</b>.","Before Selly, human couriers (manual testers) walked the mall for every delivery, every day. Selly walks it the same way a human does, but faster, and never gets tired."],"why":["<b>What:</b> Selenium is an open-source suite that controls a real browser from code, using the W3C WebDriver protocol.","<b>Why:</b> a project releases every sprint, and a manual regression of 500 test cases takes days. Automated Selenium tests run on Chrome, Firefox and Edge in CI after every commit and report failures in minutes."],"obj":["Understand what Selenium is and why it dominates test automation","Differentiate Selenium IDE, WebDriver, and Grid 4","Visualize W3C WebDriver architecture flow","Compare Selenium vs Cypress vs Playwright vs Puppeteer"],"theory":["Selenium is an open-source umbrella project for browser automation. Its core, Selenium WebDriver, implements the W3C WebDriver standard — a remote control interface for browsers. Every command you write in Java becomes a JSON payload sent over HTTP to a browser-specific driver (chromedriver, geckodriver), which then executes it natively.","Selenium IDE is a Chrome/Firefox extension for record-and-playback prototyping. WebDriver is the programming interface (Java, Python, C# etc). Selenium Grid 4 allows parallel, distributed execution across multiple OS/browser combinations via Hub/Node or fully distributed Router/Distributor model.","Unlike Cypress or Playwright which inject scripts inside browser, Selenium drives the browser externally — meaning real user-like interactions, multiple tabs/windows, and support for mobile via Appium. The trade-off is slightly slower execution and need to handle waits explicitly."],"pts":["<b>Selenium IDE:</b> browser extension to record and play back; good for quick prototypes, not for large frameworks.","<b>Selenium WebDriver:</b> the core API (Java, Python, C#, JS, Ruby) that talks to a browser driver. This is what the course uses.","<b>Selenium Grid:</b> runs tests in parallel on many machines and browsers (hub and nodes, or standalone).","<b>Selenium RC:</b> the old server-based tool, deprecated and replaced by WebDriver.","<b>Vs other tools:</b> Cypress is JavaScript only and runs inside the browser; Playwright is fast with built-in auto-wait; UFT is paid and uses VBScript; Appium automates mobile apps using the WebDriver protocol. Selenium wins on language choice, browser coverage and ecosystem; you bring your own test runner (TestNG/JUnit) and reporting.","<b>Selenium 4:</b> relative locators, new window/tab API, Chrome DevTools/BiDi support, and Selenium Manager that downloads drivers for you."],"file":"Module01_Intro.java","path":"Module01_Intro.java","code":"package com.seleniumlearning.module01;\n\nimport org.openqa.selenium.WebDriver;\nimport org.openqa.selenium.chrome.ChromeDriver;\nimport io.github.bonigarcia.wdm.WebDriverManager;\n\n/**\n * Module 01 - Selenium Architecture Demo\n * This shows the fundamental WebDriver flow:\n * Client (Java) -> JSON Wire/W3C Protocol -> Driver -> Browser\n */\npublic class Module01_Intro {\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        // 1. Setup driver binary automatically\n        WebDriverManager.chromedriver().setup();\n\n        // 2. Client creates a WebDriver session (POST /session)\n        // Internally: {\"capabilities\": {\"browserName\":\"chrome\"}}\n        WebDriver driver = new ChromeDriver();\n\n        try {\n            // 3. Navigate command becomes JSON: POST /session/{id}/url\n            // Body: {\"url\": \"https://selenium.dev\"}\n            driver.get(\"https://www.selenium.dev\");\n\n            // 4. Query commands: GET /session/{id}/title\n            String title = driver.getTitle();\n            System.out.println(\"Page Title: \" + title);\n\n            // 5. Architecture validation\n            System.out.println(\"W3C WebDriver is active: \" +\n                ((ChromeDriver)driver).getCapabilities().getBrowserName());\n\n        } finally {\n            // 6. DELETE /session/{id} - terminates browser & driver\n            driver.quit();\n        }\n    }\n}","steps":[{"title":"Dependency Resolution","lines":"1-5","desc":"WebDriverManager handles driver binary download. No manual System.setProperty needed in 2024+. The client library serializes Java commands to W3C protocol."},{"title":"Session Creation","lines":"15-20","desc":"new ChromeDriver() starts chromedriver process on port 9515, then sends POST /session with desired capabilities. Server returns sessionId used for all future commands."},{"title":"Command Serialization","lines":"23-27","desc":"driver.get() is not direct navigation. It's converted to JSON payload and sent via HTTP. This decoupling is what makes Grid possible — JSON can travel over network."},{"title":"State Query","lines":"30-33","desc":"getTitle() does GET /title. WebDriver is stateless HTTP. Each command is independent request. This explains why you need explicit waits — client doesn't know page load state automatically."},{"title":"Session Teardown","lines":"38-41","desc":"quit() sends DELETE /session. Closes all windows and kills driver process. close() only closes current window. Always use quit() in finally block."}],"snip":["// Architecture in one line\n// Test script (Java) -> Selenium client library -> browser driver -> real browser"],"best":["Always use W3C compliant capabilities (browserName, platformName) not legacy JSONWP.","Treat WebDriver as remote control, not in-browser library — handle synchronization explicitly.","Use Grid 4 for parallel execution from day one, even locally via docker: selenium/standalone-chrome."],"bad":["Thinking Selenium IDE code is production-ready. It's for prototyping only.","Not understanding that driver.get() is async over HTTP — assuming page is loaded immediately.","Mixing implicit waits with explicit waits causes unpredictable timeouts.","Selenium automates <b>web browsers only</b>. Desktop apps, captchas, barcodes and OTP are out of scope.","Commonly asked: difference between Selenium 3 and 4, and what Grid is for."],"sim":["[WD Manager] Resolving chromedriver 126.0.6478.127...","[Driver] Starting ChromeDriver 126.0.6478.127 on port 9515","[HTTP] POST /session {capabilities:{browserName:chrome}} -> 200 {sessionId: a1b2c3}","[HTTP] POST /session/a1b2c3/url {url: https://www.selenium.dev} -> 200","[HTTP] GET /session/a1b2c3/title -> {value: \"Selenium\"}","Page Title: Selenium","W3C WebDriver is active: chrome","[HTTP] DELETE /session/a1b2c3 -> Browser closed"],"extra":{"n":"Architecture flow","c":"Your test (Java)\n   |  Selenium client library (JSON commands)\n   v  HTTP  (W3C WebDriver protocol)\nBrowser driver: chromedriver / geckodriver / msedgedriver\n   |  native browser automation interface\n   v\nReal browser: Chrome / Firefox / Edge\n\nWith Grid 4: Test -> Router -> Distributor -> Node (driver + browser)"}},{"t":"Selenium Setup","s":"JARs or Maven dependency, browser drivers, and IDE configuration.","est":"30 min","lvl":"Beginner","an":["Unboxing Selly. The <b>body</b> is the Selenium library (JARs). To enter each mall brand she needs the right <b>key card</b>: the <b>browser driver</b> for Chrome, Firefox or Edge. The <b>IDE</b> is her workshop where you program her."],"why":["<b>Why:</b> code cannot control a browser alone. The driver is a small program that translates Selenium commands into browser actions. A shared, Maven-based setup means every team member and the CI server get identical versions with one command."],"obj":["Configure JDK 17, Maven, IntelliJ for Selenium 4","Understand pom.xml dependencies and transitive deps","Compare WebDriverManager vs manual driver management","Create professional project structure"],"theory":["Prerequisites: JDK 17 LTS (Selenium 4.22+ requires Java 11 minimum but 17 recommended), Maven 3.9+, IntelliJ IDEA Community. Selenium 4 uses W3C protocol by default, no need for DesiredCapabilities for basic launch.","Maven central artifact is org.seleniumhq.selenium:selenium-java:4.22.0 — it pulls api, chrome, firefox, edge, etc transitively. Add WebDriverManager 5.6.2 to avoid manual driver binaries. SLF4J simple for clean logs.","Manual setup with System.setProperty('webdriver.chrome.driver', path) is fragile — version mismatch breaks CI. WebDriverManager checks browser version at runtime and downloads matching driver to ~/.cache/selenium. For corporate proxies, configure wdm.proxy."],"pts":["Install <b>JDK 11 or 17</b>, an IDE (IntelliJ IDEA or Eclipse) and a browser.","Create a <b>Maven project</b> and add <code>selenium-java</code> plus <code>testng</code> in <code>pom.xml</code>. Maven downloads all transitive JARs.","Without Maven: download the Selenium Java zip, then add all JARs through <i>Build Path &gt; Add External JARs</i>.","<b>Drivers:</b> chromedriver, geckodriver, msedgedriver. Since Selenium 4.6, <b>Selenium Manager</b> finds or downloads the matching driver automatically. Older code used <code>System.setProperty(\"webdriver.chrome.driver\",\"path\")</code>.","Driver version must match the browser version, otherwise you get <code>SessionNotCreatedException</code>."],"file":"SetupManager.java","path":"setup/SetupManager.java","code":"package com.seleniumlearning.setup;\n\nimport io.github.bonigarcia.wdm.WebDriverManager;\nimport org.openqa.selenium.WebDriver;\nimport org.openqa.selenium.chrome.ChromeDriver;\nimport org.openqa.selenium.chrome.ChromeOptions;\nimport org.openqa.selenium.edge.EdgeDriver;\nimport org.openqa.selenium.firefox.FirefoxDriver;\n\nimport java.time.Duration;\n\npublic class SetupManager {\n\n    public enum BrowserType { CHROME, FIREFOX, EDGE }\n\n    // Factory that hides setup complexity\n    public static WebDriver createDriver(BrowserType type, boolean headless) {\n        switch (type) {\n            case CHROME:\n                WebDriverManager.chromedriver().setup();\n                ChromeOptions chromeOpts = new ChromeOptions();\n                chromeOpts.addArguments(\"--start-maximized\");\n                chromeOpts.addArguments(\"--disable-notifications\");\n                if (headless) chromeOpts.addArguments(\"--headless=new\");\n                // Selenium 4.10+ supports --remote-allow-origins fix internally\n                return new ChromeDriver(chromeOpts);\n            case FIREFOX:\n                WebDriverManager.firefoxdriver().setup();\n                return new FirefoxDriver();\n            case EDGE:\n                WebDriverManager.edgedriver().setup();\n                return new EdgeDriver();\n            default:\n                throw new IllegalArgumentException(\"Browser not supported: \" + type);\n        }\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        WebDriver driver = createDriver(BrowserType.CHROME, false);\n        driver.manage().timeouts().implicitlyWait(Duration.ofSeconds(0));\n        // Note: We set implicit to 0 to prefer explicit waits (Module 9)\n        try {\n            driver.get(\"https://example.com\");\n            System.out.println(\"Browser launched: \" + driver.getTitle());\n        } finally {\n            driver.quit();\n        }\n    }\n}","steps":[{"title":"Driver Resolution Strategy","lines":"1-13","desc":"WebDriverManager uses browser version detection via command line (google-chrome --version). It downloads correct driver to cache, avoiding 'session not created: This version only supports Chrome version X' errors."},{"title":"Options Pattern","lines":"16-25","desc":"ChromeOptions is the W3C way to set args, prefs, experimental options. --start-maximized and --disable-notifications are must-have for stable tests. headless=new uses new Headless Chrome that supports extensions."},{"title":"Factory Encapsulation","lines":"15-34","desc":"Static factory returns WebDriver interface, not concrete class. This enables cross-browser testing by changing one enum. Keeps System.setProperty out of tests."},{"title":"Timeout Strategy","lines":"37-38","desc":"Setting implicit wait to 0 is modern best practice. Mixing implicit and explicit waits causes multiplied timeouts. We'll use explicit waits exclusively from Module 9."},{"title":"Resource Management","lines":"39-45","desc":"Always wrap driver in try-finally with quit(). For TestNG/JUnit you'd use @AfterMethod, but even in main() this pattern prevents orphan chromedriver processes."}],"snip":["<dependencies>\n  <dependency>\n    <groupId>org.seleniumhq.selenium</groupId>\n    <artifactId>selenium-java</artifactId>\n    <version>4.25.0</version> <!-- use the latest 4.x -->\n  </dependency>\n  <dependency>\n    <groupId>org.testng</groupId>\n    <artifactId>testng</artifactId>\n    <version>7.10.2</version>\n    <scope>test</scope>\n  </dependency>\n</dependencies>"],"best":["Use WebDriverManager with .cachePath(\"./drivers\") for CI caching. Never commit driver binaries.","Create DriverFactory with ThreadLocal&lt;WebDriver&gt; for parallel execution later.","Pin selenium-java version via &lt;properties&gt; in pom.xml for easy upgrades."],"bad":["Using System.setProperty with absolute path C:\\drivers\\chromedriver.exe — breaks on teammate's Mac/Linux.","Adding both selenium-java and selenium-chrome-driver separately — causes version conflict. Use selenium-java only.","Leaving implicit wait at 10s default — makes explicit waits slow and flaky.","Never commit driver binaries to Git; rely on Selenium Manager or WebDriverManager.","Check the Java version (<code>java -version</code>) when the IDE shows compile errors."],"sim":["[Maven] Resolving selenium-java:4.22.0 ... 14 transitive deps","[WDM] Detected chrome version 126.0.6478.127","[WDM] Using chromedriver 126.0.6478.127 (cached at ~/.cache/selenium)","[Driver] ChromeOptions: [start-maximized, disable-notifications]","[HTTP] POST /session -> 200 session=9f8e7d","Browser launched: Example Domain","[HTTP] DELETE /session/9f8e7d"],"extra":{"n":"pom.xml","c":"<project xmlns=\"http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0\">\n  <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>\n  <groupId>com.seleniumlearning</groupId>\n  <artifactId>selenium-java-mastery</artifactId>\n  <version>1.0</version>\n  <properties>\n    <maven.compiler.source>17</maven.compiler.source>\n    <maven.compiler.target>17</maven.compiler.target>\n    <selenium.version>4.22.0</selenium.version>\n  </properties>\n  <dependencies>\n    <dependency>\n      <groupId>org.seleniumhq.selenium</groupId>\n      <artifactId>selenium-java</artifactId>\n      <version>${selenium.version}</version>\n    </dependency>\n    <dependency>\n      <groupId>io.github.bonigarcia</groupId>\n      <artifactId>webdrivermanager</artifactId>\n      <version>5.6.2</version>\n    </dependency>\n    <dependency>\n      <groupId>org.slf4j</groupId>\n      <artifactId>slf4j-simple</artifactId>\n      <version>2.0.13</version>\n    </dependency>\n  </dependencies>\n</project>"}},{"t":"WebDriver Basics","s":"Launching a browser, navigation commands and browser commands.","est":"35 min","lvl":"Beginner","an":["Selly walks to the mall <b>entrance</b> (<code>get</code>), steps back or forward through corridors (<code>back/forward</code>), reads the <b>mall notice board</b> (<code>getTitle</code>), and finally leaves: closing one door (<code>close</code>) or switching off the whole mall visit (<code>quit</code>)."],"why":["<b>What:</b> <code>WebDriver</code> is an interface; <code>ChromeDriver</code>, <code>FirefoxDriver</code> and <code>EdgeDriver</code> implement it. <b>Why:</b> coding to the interface lets you switch browsers by changing one line, which is how cross-browser testing is done in real projects."],"obj":["Master browser launch, navigation, and window management","Differentiate close() vs quit(), get() vs navigate().to()","Use getTitle, getCurrentUrl, getPageSource effectively","Handle window sizing and positioning"],"theory":["WebDriver is an interface, ChromeDriver/FirefoxDriver are implementations. The interface defines 13+ methods: get, getTitle, findElement, etc. navigate() returns Navigation interface with to(), back(), forward(), refresh() — to() keeps browser history, get() waits for page load by default.","close() closes current window handle only; if it's last window, it quits browser but driver process may remain. quit() closes all windows, ends session, kills driver process. Always use quit(). getCurrentUrl() after navigation verifies redirect chains. getPageSource() returns raw HTML after JS execution — useful for debugging but not for assertions (use WebElement text).","manage().window() gives Window interface: maximize(), fullscreen(), setSize(Dimension), getSize(). For responsive testing, setSize(new Dimension(390, 844)) to simulate iPhone. manage().timeouts() and manage().cookies() also live here."],"pts":["<code>WebDriver driver = new ChromeDriver();</code> opens a fresh browser session.","<b>Navigation:</b> <code>driver.get(url)</code> waits for page load; <code>navigate().to(url)</code>, <code>back()</code>, <code>forward()</code>, <code>refresh()</code> keep history.","<b>Browser commands:</b> <code>getTitle()</code>, <code>getCurrentUrl()</code>, <code>getPageSource()</code>, <code>getWindowHandle()</code>.","<b>Window:</b> <code>manage().window().maximize()</code>, <code>minimize()</code>, <code>fullscreen()</code>, <code>setSize(new Dimension(w,h))</code>.","<b>close()</b> closes the current window; <b>quit()</b> closes all windows and ends the session."],"file":"BrowserLaunchDemo.java","path":"module03/BrowserLaunchDemo.java","code":"package com.seleniumlearning.module03;\n\nimport org.openqa.selenium.Dimension;\nimport org.openqa.selenium.WebDriver;\nimport org.openqa.selenium.chrome.ChromeDriver;\nimport io.github.bonigarcia.wdm.WebDriverManager;\n\npublic class BrowserLaunchDemo {\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws InterruptedException {\n        WebDriverManager.chromedriver().setup();\n        WebDriver driver = new ChromeDriver();\n\n        try {\n            // --- Window Commands ---\n            driver.manage().window().maximize();\n            System.out.println(\"Window maximized\");\n\n            // --- Navigation Methods ---\n            // get() waits for page load (document.readyState = complete)\n            driver.get(\"https://www.google.com\");\n            System.out.println(\"Title after get(): \" + driver.getTitle());\n\n            // navigate().to() does NOT wait automatically, keeps history\n            driver.navigate().to(\"https://www.selenium.dev\");\n            System.out.println(\"URL after navigate: \" + driver.getCurrentUrl());\n\n            // Browser history simulation\n            driver.navigate().back();   // back to Google\n            Thread.sleep(1000);\n            System.out.println(\"After back: \" + driver.getTitle());\n\n            driver.navigate().forward(); // forward to Selenium\n            driver.navigate().refresh(); // F5\n\n            // --- Browser Info Commands ---\n            String title = driver.getTitle();\n            String currentUrl = driver.getCurrentUrl();\n            String pageSourceSnippet = driver.getPageSource().substring(0, 200);\n\n            System.out.println(\"Title length: \" + title.length());\n            System.out.println(\"URL contains selenium: \" + currentUrl.contains(\"selenium\"));\n            System.out.println(\"Page source preview: \" + pageSourceSnippet);\n\n            // --- Window Size Control (Responsive testing) ---\n            driver.manage().window().setSize(new Dimension(1280, 800));\n            Dimension size = driver.manage().window().getSize();\n            System.out.println(\"Set size to: \" + size.getWidth() + \"x\" + size.getHeight());\n\n        } finally {\n            // close() vs quit() demo - using quit for cleanup\n            driver.quit();\n        }\n    }\n}","steps":[{"title":"Driver Instantiation","lines":"8-10","desc":"ChromeDriver() without args launches visible browser. For CI you'd pass ChromeOptions headless. WebDriverManager ensures binary compatibility."},{"title":"Window Management","lines":"13-15","desc":"maximize() uses OS window manager. On Linux headless, it may not work — use setSize instead. Always maximize to avoid element not clickable due to responsive hide."},{"title":"Navigation Flow","lines":"18-30","desc":"get() vs navigate().to(): get() waits for page load event. to() is for history manipulation. back()/forward() mimic browser buttons, useful for testing SPA routing."},{"title":"Inspection Commands","lines":"33-40","desc":"getTitle() and getCurrentUrl() are lightweight. getPageSource() is heavy — returns entire DOM. Don't assert using pageSource; use explicit element locators."},{"title":"Responsive Control","lines":"43-46","desc":"setSize lets you test mobile breakpoints without device emulation. Combine with Chrome DevTools emulation for true mobile testing (Module 12)."}],"snip":["WebDriver driver = new ChromeDriver();\ndriver.manage().window().maximize();\ndriver.get(\"https://example.com/login\");\nSystem.out.println(driver.getTitle());\nSystem.out.println(driver.getCurrentUrl());\ndriver.navigate().to(\"https://example.com/cart\");\ndriver.navigate().back();\ndriver.navigate().refresh();\ndriver.quit();"],"best":["Use navigate().to() when you need to test back/forward cache behavior; get() for fresh navigation.","Always log currentUrl after navigation to catch unexpected redirects (login pages).","Set window size explicitly in @BeforeMethod to make tests resolution-independent."],"bad":["Calling close() in loop for multiple windows without switching handles — closes same window repeatedly.","Using Thread.sleep for navigation wait. Use explicit wait for title or URL instead.","Forgetting that getPageSource() returns after JS execution, not initial HTML — leads to flaky string checks.","Always call <code>quit()</code> in <code>@AfterMethod</code>/<code>finally</code>; otherwise orphan browser processes pile up on CI.","Interview: <code>get()</code> vs <code>navigate().to()</code> (same result; navigate keeps history and offers back/forward)."],"sim":["[Window] maximize() -> 1920x1080","[HTTP] POST /url {https://www.google.com} -> 200","Title after get(): Google","[HTTP] POST /url {https://www.selenium.dev} -> 200","URL after navigate: https://www.selenium.dev/","[HTTP] POST /back -> 200","After back: Google","[HTTP] POST /forward -> 200, POST /refresh -> 200","Title length: 8","Set size to: 1280x800"]},{"t":"Locators in Selenium","s":"ID, Name, ClassName, TagName, LinkText, PartialLinkText, XPath, CSS Selector.","est":"40 min","lvl":"Beginner","an":["Every shop in the mall needs an <b>address</b> so Selly can find it. <b>ID</b> = unique shop licence number. <b>Name</b> = shop name. <b>ClassName</b> = category sign (all \"Cafe\" shops). <b>TagName</b> = type of unit. <b>LinkText</b> = text on the signboard. <b>XPath</b> and <b>CSS</b> = detailed directions."],"why":["<b>What:</b> a locator tells Selenium which element on the DOM to act on. <b>Why:</b> every test step (type here, click there) starts with finding the right element; unstable locators are the number one reason automation suites break."],"obj":["Master all 8 Selenium locators with priority order","Identify unique locators using DevTools","Handle dynamic IDs and compound classes","Choose locator strategy for stability"],"theory":["Locators are the backbone — findElement(By.id('')) is the most common command. 8 locators: id (fastest, unique), name, className (single class only), tagName, linkText (exact anchor text), partialLinkText, cssSelector, xpath. Priority: ID &gt; Name &gt; CSS &gt; XPath &gt; others. ID is fastest because browsers have native getElementById.","In DevTools Elements tab, Ctrl+F opens search. Type CSS or XPath to test. $0 is selected element. $x('//div') evaluates XPath. For uniqueness, id should appear once; className may match many — use CSS if multiple classes. linkText only works on &lt;a&gt; tags, case-sensitive.","Dynamic IDs like id='user_1234_xyz' break tests. Avoid them. If no ID, ask dev to add data-testid attribute and use CSS [data-testid='login']. That's most stable. Compound class 'btn btn-primary' cannot be used with By.className('btn btn-primary') — it expects single class. Use By.cssSelector('.btn.btn-primary') instead."],"pts":["<code>By.id(\"email\")</code>: fastest and best when unique.","<code>By.name(\"q\")</code>, <code>By.className(\"btn\")</code> (single class only, no spaces), <code>By.tagName(\"a\")</code>.","<code>By.linkText(\"Sign in\")</code> and <code>By.partialLinkText(\"Sign\")</code> work only on <code>&lt;a&gt;</code> tags.","<code>By.xpath(...)</code> and <code>By.cssSelector(...)</code> handle everything else.","<b>Priority:</b> id &gt; name &gt; CSS &gt; XPath &gt; others.","<code>findElement</code> returns the first match or throws <code>NoSuchElementException</code>; <code>findElements</code> returns a list (empty if none, no exception).","<b>Selenium 4 relative locators:</b> <code>with(By.tagName(\"input\")).below(label)</code>, also <code>above, toLeftOf, toRightOf, near</code>."],"file":"LocatorsDemo.java","path":"module04/LocatorsDemo.java","code":"package com.seleniumlearning.module04;\n\nimport org.openqa.selenium.By;\nimport org.openqa.selenium.WebDriver;\nimport org.openqa.selenium.WebElement;\nimport org.openqa.selenium.chrome.ChromeDriver;\nimport io.github.bonigarcia.wdm.WebDriverManager;\n\npublic class LocatorsDemo {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        WebDriverManager.chromedriver().setup();\n        WebDriver driver = new ChromeDriver();\n        driver.get(\"https://practicetestautomation.com/practice-test-login/\");\n\n        // 1. ID - fastest, most stable\n        WebElement usernameById = driver.findElement(By.id(\"username\"));\n        usernameById.sendKeys(\"student\");\n\n        // 2. Name attribute\n        WebElement usernameByName = driver.findElement(By.name(\"username\"));\n        // usernameByName.clear();\n\n        // 3. ClassName - single class only!\n        // Page has class \"btn\" - but if multiple classes, use CSS\n        WebElement submitBtnByClass = driver.findElement(By.className(\"btn\"));\n        // Works because btn is unique here. For 'btn btn-primary' would fail.\n\n        // 4. TagName - useful for counting elements\n        java.util.List<WebElement> allInputs = driver.findElements(By.tagName(\"input\"));\n        System.out.println(\"Total inputs on page: \" + allInputs.size());\n\n        // 5. LinkText - exact match, only <a> tags\n        // WebElement link = driver.findElement(By.linkText(\"Test Login Page\"));\n\n        // 6. PartialLinkText\n        // WebElement partialLink = driver.findElement(By.partialLinkText(\"Test Login\"));\n\n        // 7. CSS Selector - powerful, faster than XPath\n        WebElement passwordByCss = driver.findElement(By.cssSelector(\"input#password\"));\n        passwordByCss.sendKeys(\"Password123\");\n\n        // CSS with attribute\n        WebElement submitByCssAttr = driver.findElement(By.cssSelector(\"button[type='submit']\"));\n\n        // 8. XPath - most flexible, can traverse DOM both ways\n        WebElement usernameByXpath = driver.findElement(By.xpath(\"//input[@id='username']\"));\n\n        // XPath with text()\n        WebElement headingByXpath = driver.findElement(By.xpath(\"//h2[text()='Test login']\"));\n\n        System.out.println(\"Heading: \" + headingByXpath.getText());\n\n        // Best practice: prefer ID > CSS > XPath\n        driver.quit();\n    }\n}","steps":[{"title":"ID Locator - Gold Standard","lines":"14-16","desc":"By.id maps to document.getElementById — O(1) lookup. If dev provides stable IDs, always use them. Check uniqueness in DevTools: $('#username') should return 1 element."},{"title":"Name &amp; ClassName Caveats","lines":"18-27","desc":"Name can be duplicate (radio groups). className only accepts single class. For 'form-control input-lg', By.className fails with 'Compound class names not permitted'. Use CSS .form-control.input-lg."},{"title":"TagName for Collections","lines":"29-31","desc":"findElements(By.tagName) returns List. Useful for counting links, images, or table rows. If size is 0, no exception — returns empty list. findElement throws NoSuchElementException if not found."},{"title":"LinkText Specificity","lines":"33-37","desc":"linkText works only on &lt;a&gt; tags and must match exact visible text including spaces. partialLinkText is more forgiving but risky — may match multiple links. Prefer CSS a[href*='login']."},{"title":"CSS vs XPath Decision","lines":"39-52","desc":"CSS: input#password is faster, readable, supports ID, class, attribute. XPath: can traverse up (parent), search by text(), use axes. For modern apps, CSS first, XPath only for text or sibling traversal."}],"snip":["WebElement email = driver.findElement(By.id(\"email\"));\nList<WebElement> links = driver.findElements(By.tagName(\"a\"));\nSystem.out.println(\"Links: \" + links.size());\ndriver.findElement(By.linkText(\"Forgot password?\")).click();\ndriver.findElement(By.cssSelector(\"input[name='q']\")).sendKeys(\"shoes\");"],"best":["Use data-testid attributes: By.cssSelector('[data-testid=\"submit-btn\"]') — devs can add, doesn't break with styling changes.","Never use absolute XPath /html/body/div[1]/div... — breaks with any DOM change. Always relative //.","Verify locator uniqueness in DevTools console: $$('your css').length should be 1."],"bad":["By.className('btn primary') — throws InvalidSelectorException. Use By.cssSelector('.btn.primary').","By.id with dynamic id like 'react-select-2-input' — changes on each reload. Use stable attribute.","Using XPath when CSS would work — XPath is slower in IE/old Edge and harder to read.","Use <code>findElements().size()==0</code> to check that something is absent.","Do not use auto-generated absolute XPath from the browser; it breaks with any layout change."],"sim":["[Locate] By.id: username -> FOUND (1 element)","[Locate] By.name: username -> FOUND","[Locate] By.className: btn -> FOUND","[Locate] By.tagName: input -> 2 elements","Total inputs on page: 2","[Locate] By.cssSelector: input#password -> FOUND","[Locate] By.xpath: //h2[text()='Test login'] -> FOUND","Heading: Test login","[Session] quit"]},{"t":"XPath & CSS","s":"Absolute vs relative XPath, axes, dynamic XPath, CSS selectors.","est":"50 min","lvl":"Intermediate","an":["<b>Absolute XPath</b> = directions from the main gate: \"1st floor, 2nd lane, 3rd shop\"; one new shop and Selly gets lost. <b>Relative XPath</b> = \"the shop next to the Cafe\". <b>Axes</b> = family-tree directions (parent, sibling, child). <b>Dynamic XPath</b> = shop room numbers change every week, so Selly looks for the signboard text instead. <b>CSS</b> is the short-hand version."],"why":["<b>Why:</b> real pages often lack IDs, or generate random ones like <code>btn_83921</code>. XPath and CSS let you describe an element by its attributes, text or position relative to stable neighbours."],"obj":["Write resilient relative XPath with axes","Master dynamic XPath functions: contains, starts-with, text","Use CSS attribute operators ^ $ * and combinators","Apply best practices for maintainable locators"],"theory":["Absolute XPath /html/body/div[2]/form/input[1] starts from root and is brittle. Relative XPath //input[@id='username'] starts anywhere and is stable. Always use relative. XPath axes let you navigate: parent::, child::, following-sibling::, preceding-sibling::, ancestor::, descendant:: — essential for tables where you know label but need input.","Dynamic XPath handles changing attributes: //div[contains(@class,'modal')] finds any modal variant. //button[starts-with(@id,'submit_')] for dynamic IDs. //label[text()='Email'] finds by visible text. Combine with and/or: //input[@type='text' and @required]. text() vs . : text() is direct text node, . includes descendant text.","CSS is faster: #id, .class, [attribute='value'], [attr^='starts'], [attr$='ends'], [attr*='contains']. Combinators: space (descendant), &gt; (direct child), + (adjacent sibling), ~ (general sibling). Pseudo: :first-child, :last-child, :nth-child(2), :nth-of-type(). CSS can't traverse up or search by text — that's XPath territory."],"pts":["<b>Absolute:</b> <code>/html/body/div[2]/form/input</code>. Fragile. <b>Relative:</b> <code>//input[@id='email']</code>.","<b>Functions:</b> <code>contains(@class,'btn')</code>, <code>starts-with(@id,'user_')</code>, <code>text()='Login'</code>, <code>normalize-space()</code>; combine with <code>and</code>/<code>or</code>; index with <code>[1]</code>, <code>[last()]</code>.","<b>Axes:</b> <code>parent::</code>, <code>child::</code>, <code>ancestor::</code>, <code>descendant::</code>, <code>following-sibling::</code>, <code>preceding-sibling::</code>, <code>following::</code>.","<b>Dynamic XPath:</b> <code>//input[starts-with(@id,'user_')]</code> or build it in Java with a variable: <code>\"//a[text()='\"+name+\"']\"</code>.","<b>CSS:</b> <code>#id</code>, <code>.class</code>, <code>tag.class</code>, <code>[attr='v']</code>, <code>[attr^='st']</code> (starts), <code>[attr$='nd']</code> (ends), <code>[attr*='mid']</code> (contains), <code>parent &gt; child</code>, <code>ancestor descendant</code>, <code>li:nth-child(2)</code>.","CSS cannot select by text and cannot go up to a parent; XPath can."],"file":"AdvancedLocatorsDemo.java","path":"module05/AdvancedLocatorsDemo.java","code":"package com.seleniumlearning.module05;\n\nimport org.openqa.selenium.By;\nimport org.openqa.selenium.WebDriver;\nimport org.openqa.selenium.chrome.ChromeDriver;\nimport io.github.bonigarcia.wdm.WebDriverManager;\n\npublic class AdvancedLocatorsDemo {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        WebDriverManager.chromedriver().setup();\n        WebDriver driver = new ChromeDriver();\n        driver.get(\"https://example.com/form\");\n\n        // --- XPath Axes ---\n        // Find input that is following-sibling of label with text Email\n        driver.findElement(By.xpath(\"//label[text()='Email']/following-sibling::input\"));\n\n        // Parent axis: find form that is parent of this input\n        driver.findElement(By.xpath(\"//input[@id='email']/parent::form\"));\n\n        // Ancestor: find div with class container that contains email input\n        driver.findElement(By.xpath(\"//input[@id='email']/ancestor::div[@class='container']\"));\n\n        // Descendant: find all inputs inside form\n        driver.findElements(By.xpath(\"//form[@id='loginForm']/descendant::input\"));\n\n        // --- Dynamic XPath ---\n        // contains() for partial attribute match\n        driver.findElement(By.xpath(\"//button[contains(@class,'submit')]\"));\n        driver.findElement(By.xpath(\"//div[contains(text(),'Welcome')]\"));\n\n        // starts-with() for dynamic IDs like user_12345\n        driver.findElement(By.xpath(\"//input[starts-with(@id,'user_')]\"));\n\n        // Combining conditions with and / or\n        driver.findElement(By.xpath(\"//input[@type='text' and @name='username']\"));\n        driver.findElement(By.xpath(\"//button[@type='submit' or @type='button']\"));\n\n        // --- CSS Selectors Deep Dive ---\n        // Attribute selectors\n        driver.findElement(By.cssSelector(\"input[type='email']\"));          // exact\n        driver.findElement(By.cssSelector(\"input[id^='user_']\"));           // starts with\n        driver.findElement(By.cssSelector(\"input[id$='_field']\"));          // ends with\n        driver.findElement(By.cssSelector(\"div[class*='error']\"));           // contains\n\n        // Combinators\n        driver.findElement(By.cssSelector(\"form#login > input\"));            // direct child\n        driver.findElement(By.cssSelector(\"label + input\"));                 // adjacent sibling\n        driver.findElement(By.cssSelector(\"div.form-group ~ div\"));           // general sibling\n\n        // Pseudo-classes\n        driver.findElement(By.cssSelector(\"ul li:first-child\"));\n        driver.findElement(By.cssSelector(\"ul li:last-child\"));\n        driver.findElement(By.cssSelector(\"table tr:nth-child(2) td:nth-child(3)\"));\n        driver.findElement(By.cssSelector(\"input:checked\"));\n        driver.findElement(By.cssSelector(\"input:disabled\"));\n\n        System.out.println(\"Advanced locators executed - 20 strategies validated\");\n        driver.quit();\n    }\n}","steps":[{"title":"XPath Axes for Relationships","lines":"12-22","desc":"following-sibling:: finds elements on same level after. Essential for label-&gt;input patterns where HTML is &lt;label&gt;Email&lt;/label&gt;&lt;input&gt;. parent:: and ancestor:: traverse up — CSS can't do this."},{"title":"Dynamic Handling with Functions","lines":"25-33","desc":"contains(@class,'submit') handles class order variations 'btn submit primary' vs 'submit btn'. starts-with() solves React-generated IDs like 'downshift-0-input'. text() finds by visible label when no ID exists."},{"title":"Logical Operators","lines":"35-37","desc":"and/or combine conditions. //input[@type='text' and @required] finds required text fields only. More precise than single attribute, reduces false matches."},{"title":"CSS Attribute Operators","lines":"40-44","desc":"^= starts-with, $= ends-with, *= contains. CSS version of contains() and starts-with() but faster. Use for dynamic IDs without XPath overhead."},{"title":"Combinators &amp; Pseudos","lines":"46-55","desc":"&gt; direct child prevents matching nested elements. + adjacent sibling finds input right after label. :nth-child() is perfect for tables: tr:nth-child(2) = second row. :checked/:disabled test state without isSelected()."}],"snip":["// XPath\nBy.xpath(\"//button[normalize-space()='Add to cart']\");\nBy.xpath(\"//td[text()='Phone']/following-sibling::td/button\");\nBy.xpath(\"//label[text()='Email']/parent::div//input\");\nBy.xpath(\"//input[starts-with(@id,'user_') and @type='text']\");\n// CSS\nBy.cssSelector(\"form#login input[type='password']\");\nBy.cssSelector(\"ul.menu > li:nth-child(3) a\");\nBy.cssSelector(\"a[href*='checkout']\");"],"best":["Build XPath from nearest stable anchor: //h2[text()='Login']/following::form — anchor text rarely changes.","Use CSS for 80% cases, XPath only when you need text() or traversing up. CSS is 10-30% faster.","Create locator builder utility: byTestId('login') returns [data-testid='login'] to enforce consistency."],"bad":["//*[contains(text(),'Submit')] — * checks every node, slow. Use //button[contains(...)].","Using index //div[3] — breaks when new div added. Use semantic attribute instead.","CSS: div &gt; * — wildcard child is unpredictable. Be specific: div &gt; input.","Test locators in DevTools Console: <code>$x(\"//...\")</code> for XPath and <code>$$(\"css\")</code> for CSS.","Interview: XPath <code>//</code> vs <code>/</code>; <code>contains()</code> vs <code>starts-with()</code>; which is faster, CSS or XPath (CSS slightly, rarely matters)."],"sim":["[XPath] //label[text()='Email']/following-sibling::input -> FOUND","[XPath] //input[@id='email']/parent::form -> FOUND","[XPath] //button[contains(@class,'submit')] -> FOUND (2 matches, using first)","[CSS] input[id^='user_'] -> FOUND","[CSS] form#login > input -> 3 elements","[CSS] table tr:nth-child(2) td:nth-child(3) -> FOUND text: $25.00","Advanced locators executed - 20 strategies validated"]},{"t":"WebElement Actions","s":"click(), sendKeys(), clear(), getText(), getAttribute() and friends.","est":"30 min","lvl":"Beginner","an":["Once Selly finds a shop she needs <b>hands and eyes</b>: press the doorbell (<code>click</code>), fill the delivery form (<code>sendKeys</code>), erase a wrong entry (<code>clear</code>), read the sign (<code>getText</code>), and read a small hidden tag on the door (<code>getAttribute</code>)."],"why":["<b>What:</b> methods of the <code>WebElement</code> interface that simulate a user. <b>Why:</b> a login, search or checkout test is nothing but a sequence of these actions followed by reading results to assert them."],"obj":["Use core WebElement methods: click, sendKeys, clear, getText","Retrieve attributes, CSS values, and state","Validate element visibility and enablement","Handle input formatting and special keys"],"theory":["WebElement represents an element in DOM. After findElement, you interact via methods. click() scrolls into view and clicks center of element — fails if overlapped (use JSExecutor). sendKeys() types, but doesn't clear by default — call clear() first for edit fields. getText() returns visible text (excludes hidden via CSS), getAttribute('value') gets input value, getAttribute('innerHTML') gets HTML.","getCssValue('color') returns computed style (rgba). isDisplayed() checks if element is rendered (not display:none or hidden parent). isEnabled() checks disabled attribute — false for &lt;button disabled&gt;. isSelected() for checkboxes/radios. getTagName(), getSize(), getLocation() for geometry.","sendKeys supports Keys enum: Keys.ENTER, Keys.TAB, Keys.CONTROL+\"a\". For file upload, sendKeys(filePath) to &lt;input type='file'&gt;. clear() may not trigger change events — send Keys.CONTROL+\"a\", Keys.DELETE as alternative."],"pts":["<code>click()</code>, <code>submit()</code> (only inside a form).","<code>sendKeys(\"text\")</code> types; <code>sendKeys(Keys.ENTER)</code> presses keys; on <code>&lt;input type=file&gt;</code> it uploads a file path.","<code>clear()</code> empties a field.","<code>getText()</code> returns <b>visible</b> text only. <code>getAttribute(\"value\")</code> returns what is typed in an input. Newer versions also offer <code>getDomProperty()</code>.","<b>State checks:</b> <code>isDisplayed()</code>, <code>isEnabled()</code>, <code>isSelected()</code>; also <code>getTagName()</code>, <code>getCssValue(\"color\")</code>, <code>getSize()</code>, <code>getLocation()</code>."],"file":"ElementActionsDemo.java","path":"module06/ElementActionsDemo.java","code":"package com.seleniumlearning.module06;\n\nimport org.openqa.selenium.By;\nimport org.openqa.selenium.Keys;\nimport org.openqa.selenium.WebDriver;\nimport org.openqa.selenium.WebElement;\nimport org.openqa.selenium.chrome.ChromeDriver;\nimport io.github.bonigarcia.wdm.WebDriverManager;\n\npublic class ElementActionsDemo {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        WebDriverManager.chromedriver().setup();\n        WebDriver driver = new ChromeDriver();\n        driver.get(\"https://practicetestautomation.com/practice-test-login/\");\n\n        WebElement username = driver.findElement(By.id(\"username\"));\n        WebElement password = driver.findElement(By.id(\"password\"));\n        WebElement submitBtn = driver.findElement(By.id(\"submit\"));\n\n        // --- Input Actions ---\n        username.clear(); // Clears existing value\n        username.sendKeys(\"student\");\n        System.out.println(\"Username value attr: \" + username.getAttribute(\"value\"));\n\n        // Clear alternative that triggers events\n        password.sendKeys(Keys.CONTROL + \"a\");\n        password.sendKeys(Keys.DELETE);\n        password.sendKeys(\"Password123\");\n\n        // --- Click Action ---\n        System.out.println(\"Button displayed: \" + submitBtn.isDisplayed());\n        System.out.println(\"Button enabled: \" + submitBtn.isEnabled());\n        System.out.println(\"Button tag: \" + submitBtn.getTagName());\n        System.out.println(\"Button text: \" + submitBtn.getText());\n\n        // --- CSS & Attribute ---\n        String bgColor = submitBtn.getCssValue(\"background-color\");\n        String btnType = submitBtn.getAttribute(\"type\");\n        System.out.println(\"BG Color: \" + bgColor + \", Type: \" + btnType);\n\n        // --- Size & Location ---\n        System.out.println(\"Size: \" + submitBtn.getSize());\n        System.out.println(\"Location: \" + submitBtn.getLocation());\n\n        submitBtn.click();\n\n        // After navigation\n        WebElement successHeader = driver.findElement(By.tagName(\"h1\"));\n        System.out.println(\"Success text: \" + successHeader.getText());\n\n        driver.quit();\n    }\n}","steps":[{"title":"Clearing &amp; Typing","lines":"15-24","desc":"clear() removes value but may not fire onchange. Ctrl+A + Delete triggers keyboard events, better for React controlled inputs. getAttribute('value') verifies typing worked — getText() returns empty for inputs."},{"title":"State Validation Before Click","lines":"26-30","desc":"Always check isDisplayed() and isEnabled() before click to avoid ElementNotInteractableException. getTagName() useful for generic methods that work on button or a."},{"title":"CSS Value Extraction","lines":"32-35","desc":"getCssValue returns computed style, e.g., rgba(0, 123, 255, 1). Useful to assert error state (red border) or active state. getAttribute returns HTML attribute, not computed style."},{"title":"Geometry","lines":"37-39","desc":"getSize() and getLocation() help debug overlapping elements. If click fails with 'other element would receive click', log location of blocker element."},{"title":"Post-Action Verification","lines":"41-44","desc":"After click, wait for new element (Module 9) then getText(). Text includes visible text only — hidden elements return empty. For hidden, use getAttribute('textContent')."}],"snip":["WebElement user = driver.findElement(By.id(\"username\"));\nuser.clear();\nuser.sendKeys(\"selly@mall.com\");\nString typed = user.getAttribute(\"value\");\nWebElement btn = driver.findElement(By.id(\"login\"));\nif (btn.isDisplayed() && btn.isEnabled()) btn.click();\nString msg = driver.findElement(By.cssSelector(\".toast\")).getText();\n// upload\ndriver.findElement(By.id(\"file\")).sendKeys(\"C:\\data\\invoice.pdf\");"],"best":["Wrap sendKeys with clear: element.clear(); element.sendKeys(value); or use Ctrl+A+Delete for React apps.","Log getAttribute('outerHTML') when element not found — shows actual DOM at failure time.","Use getText().trim() — often text has leading/trailing spaces or newlines."],"bad":["username.sendKeys without clear() appends to existing value — 'adminstudent' instead of 'student'.","getText() on &lt;input&gt; returns '' — use getAttribute('value') for inputs.","Clicking without scrolling — element may be below fold. Use Actions or JS scrollIntoView first.","<code>getText()</code> on a text box is empty; use <code>getAttribute(\"value\")</code>.","Hidden elements return an empty <code>getText()</code>."],"sim":["[Action] clear() id=username","[Action] sendKeys 'student' -> value=student","Username value attr: student","[Action] Ctrl+A + Delete on password field","Button displayed: true, enabled: true, tag: button, text: Submit","BG Color: rgba(0, 123, 255, 1), Type: submit","Size: (100, 38), Location: (500, 300)","[Action] click() id=submit -> Navigation to /logged-in-successfully/","Success text: Logged In Successfully"]},{"t":"Handling Web Elements","s":"Buttons, text boxes, checkboxes, radio buttons and links in practice.","est":"35 min","lvl":"Beginner","an":["Each counter in the mall works differently: a <b>button</b> is a doorbell, a <b>text box</b> is a form line, a <b>checkbox</b> is a tick-list where many can be ticked, a <b>radio button</b> is a one-token choice box where picking one cancels the others."],"why":["<b>Why:</b> forms in real apps (registration, booking, checkout) mix all these controls. Knowing each one's behaviour prevents wrong clicks such as un-ticking a box you wanted ticked."],"obj":["Handle buttons, textboxes, links, images","Work with checkboxes and radio buttons using isSelected","Iterate over groups of elements","Handle disabled and hidden elements"],"theory":["Textboxes: clear then sendKeys. Buttons: click. Links: click or getAttribute('href') to validate URL without navigation. Images: getAttribute('src'), check naturalWidth via JSExecutor for broken images. Checkboxes and radios are &lt;input type='checkbox'&gt; — click toggles, but use isSelected() to verify state before clicking to avoid unchecking.","For groups (multiple checkboxes with same name), findElements returns List. Loop and click based on value attribute. Radio buttons: only one can be selected per name group — findElements then click desired one. If isSelected already true, skip click.","Disabled elements: isEnabled() returns false, click throws. Hidden elements: isDisplayed() false — cannot interact via WebDriver, need JSExecutor (Module 12). Always check count via findElements before interaction — if 0, element not present."],"pts":["<b>Text box:</b> <code>clear()</code> then <code>sendKeys()</code>.","<b>Checkbox:</b> check <code>isSelected()</code> before clicking, since a click toggles.","<b>Radio:</b> clicking selects it; clicking again does not deselect.","<b>Link or button:</b> <code>click()</code>. If it opens a new page, wait or assert the URL/title afterwards.","<b>Many similar elements:</b> use <code>findElements</code> and loop.","<b>Disabled elements</b> throw <code>ElementNotInteractableException</code>; check <code>isEnabled()</code>."],"file":"WebElementsHandlingDemo.java","path":"module07/WebElementsHandlingDemo.java","code":"package com.seleniumlearning.module07;\n\nimport org.openqa.selenium.By;\nimport org.openqa.selenium.WebDriver;\nimport org.openqa.selenium.WebElement;\nimport org.openqa.selenium.chrome.ChromeDriver;\nimport io.github.bonigarcia.wdm.WebDriverManager;\nimport java.util.List;\n\npublic class WebElementsHandlingDemo {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        WebDriverManager.chromedriver().setup();\n        WebDriver driver = new ChromeDriver();\n        driver.get(\"https://the-internet.herokuapp.com/checkboxes\");\n\n        // --- Checkboxes Handling ---\n        List<WebElement> checkboxes = driver.findElements(By.cssSelector(\"input[type='checkbox']\"));\n        System.out.println(\"Found checkboxes: \" + checkboxes.size());\n\n        for (WebElement cb : checkboxes) {\n            boolean isChecked = cb.isSelected();\n            System.out.println(\"Checkbox selected: \" + isChecked);\n            if (!isChecked) {\n                cb.click(); // Check it if unchecked\n            }\n        }\n\n        // --- Radio Buttons (on another page) ---\n        driver.get(\"https://the-internet.herokuapp.com/\");\n        // Navigate to radio example or use local HTML\n        // Example logic for radio group:\n        // List<WebElement> radios = driver.findElements(By.name(\"gender\"));\n        // for (WebElement radio : radios) {\n        //     if (radio.getAttribute(\"value\").equals(\"male\") && !radio.isSelected()) {\n        //         radio.click();\n        //     }\n        // }\n\n        // --- Links & Images ---\n        driver.get(\"https://example.com\");\n        List<WebElement> links = driver.findElements(By.tagName(\"a\"));\n        for (WebElement link : links) {\n            System.out.println(\"Link: \" + link.getText() + \" -> \" + link.getAttribute(\"href\"));\n        }\n\n        // Check if image is displayed and src\n        WebElement img = driver.findElement(By.tagName(\"img\"));\n        if (img.isDisplayed()) {\n            System.out.println(\"Image src: \" + img.getAttribute(\"src\"));\n            System.out.println(\"Image alt: \" + img.getAttribute(\"alt\"));\n        }\n\n        // --- Disabled Element Check ---\n        // WebElement disabledBtn = driver.findElement(By.id(\"disabledBtn\"));\n        // if (disabledBtn.isEnabled()) {\n        //     disabledBtn.click();\n        // } else {\n        //     System.out.println(\"Button is disabled - cannot click\");\n        // }\n\n        driver.quit();\n    }\n}","steps":[{"title":"Checkbox Group Iteration","lines":"14-24","desc":"findElements returns List — iterate. isSelected() tells current state. Only click if not already selected to make test idempotent (re-runnable). Checking size first prevents NoSuchElement."},{"title":"Radio Button Logic","lines":"27-36","desc":"Radios share name attribute. Loop through group, match desired value via getAttribute('value'), check isSelected to avoid redundant click. After click, only one in group remains selected."},{"title":"Link Harvesting","lines":"39-44","desc":"Get all &lt;a&gt; tags, log text + href. Useful for broken link checker: get href, then open via HttpURLConnection to verify 200. Don't click each link — would navigate away, losing context."},{"title":"Image Validation","lines":"46-52","desc":"isDisplayed() checks if image rendered. getAttribute('src') gives URL. To check broken image, use JSExecutor: return arguments[0].naturalWidth &gt; 0. Broken images have naturalWidth 0."},{"title":"Disabled Guard","lines":"54-61","desc":"isEnabled() checks disabled attribute. Attempting click on disabled throws ElementNotInteractable. Guard with if(isEnabled()) or assert that button becomes enabled after filling form."}],"snip":["WebElement terms = driver.findElement(By.id(\"terms\"));\nif (!terms.isSelected()) terms.click();\n\nList<WebElement> radios = driver.findElements(By.name(\"gender\"));\nfor (WebElement r : radios)\n  if (r.getAttribute(\"value\").equals(\"female\")) { r.click(); break; }\n\n// tick all checkboxes\nfor (WebElement c : driver.findElements(By.cssSelector(\"input[type='checkbox']\")))\n  if (!c.isSelected()) c.click();"],"best":["For checkboxes, create helper: setCheckbox(By, boolean shouldBeChecked) that checks isSelected before clicking.","Use findElements and check size &gt; 0 instead of try-catch for optional elements — faster and cleaner.","Log getAttribute('outerHTML') for failed elements to debug in CI screenshots."],"bad":["Clicking checkbox without checking isSelected — toggles off if already checked, causing false negative.","Using click() on disabled element expecting no error — it throws exception, need guard.","findElement for group — only gets first. Use findElements for counting or iterating.","Click the visible <code>&lt;label&gt;</code> when the real checkbox is hidden by custom styling.","Assert state after an action: <code>Assert.assertTrue(terms.isSelected())</code>."],"sim":["[Locate] input[type='checkbox'] -> 2 elements","Found checkboxes: 2","Checkbox selected: false -> click()","Checkbox selected: true -> skip","[Navigation] to example.com","[Locate] tagName=a -> 1 element","Link: More information... -> https://www.iana.org/domains/example","Image src: data:image/svg+xml,... displayed: true","[Check] disabledBtn.isEnabled() -> false, skipping click"]},{"t":"Dropdown Handling","s":"Select class methods, single vs multi-select dropdowns.","est":"35 min","lvl":"Intermediate","an":["A <b>vending machine</b> in the mall. Selly can choose by the <b>label</b> printed on the button, by its <b>code</b>, or by <b>position</b>. A <b>multi-select</b> is a combo tray where she can pick several items and remove some later."],"why":["<b>Why:</b> country, state, date and category fields are dropdowns. The <code>Select</code> class gives reliable, readable methods instead of clicking and guessing."],"obj":["Use Select class for &lt;select&gt; dropdowns","Handle single vs multi-select","Get options, selected options, deselect","Handle custom (non-select) dropdowns via clicks"],"theory":["If dropdown is &lt;select&gt; tag, use org.openqa.selenium.support.ui.Select class. Constructor takes WebElement of &lt;select&gt;. Methods: selectByVisibleText('India'), selectByValue('IN'), selectByIndex(2). Index starts 0. getOptions() returns all, getAllSelectedOptions() for multi, getFirstSelectedOption() for current value.","Multi-select &lt;select multiple&gt; allows multiple selections. isMultiple() checks. You can select multiple then deselectAll() or deselectBy... Single-select throws UnsupportedOperationException on deselect methods. Always check isMultiple before multi operations.","Many modern apps use div-based custom dropdowns (React-Select, etc) not &lt;select&gt;. Select class won't work — you need to click dropdown to open, then click option by text. Use explicit wait for options to be visible after opening."],"pts":["Works only on real <code>&lt;select&gt;</code> tags: <code>new Select(element)</code>.","<b>Choose:</b> <code>selectByVisibleText</code>, <code>selectByValue</code>, <code>selectByIndex</code>.","<b>Read:</b> <code>getOptions()</code>, <code>getFirstSelectedOption()</code>, <code>getAllSelectedOptions()</code>, <code>isMultiple()</code>.","<b>Multi-select only:</b> <code>deselectAll()</code>, <code>deselectByVisibleText/Value/Index</code>. On a single select these throw <code>UnsupportedOperationException</code>.","<b>Custom dropdowns</b> (div/ul/li) are not <code>&lt;select&gt;</code>: click to open, then click the matching <code>li</code> found by text."],"file":"DropdownDemo.java","path":"module08/DropdownDemo.java","code":"package com.seleniumlearning.module08;\n\nimport org.openqa.selenium.By;\nimport org.openqa.selenium.WebDriver;\nimport org.openqa.selenium.WebElement;\nimport org.openqa.selenium.chrome.ChromeDriver;\nimport org.openqa.selenium.support.ui.Select;\nimport io.github.bonigarcia.wdm.WebDriverManager;\nimport java.util.List;\n\npublic class DropdownDemo {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        WebDriverManager.chromedriver().setup();\n        WebDriver driver = new ChromeDriver();\n        driver.get(\"https://the-internet.herokuapp.com/dropdown\");\n\n        // --- Single Select Dropdown ---\n        WebElement dropdownElement = driver.findElement(By.id(\"dropdown\"));\n        Select dropdown = new Select(dropdownElement);\n\n        System.out.println(\"Is multiple: \" + dropdown.isMultiple()); // false\n\n        // Select by visible text\n        dropdown.selectByVisibleText(\"Option 1\");\n        System.out.println(\"Selected: \" + dropdown.getFirstSelectedOption().getText());\n\n        // Select by value attribute\n        dropdown.selectByValue(\"2\");\n\n        // Select by index\n        dropdown.selectByIndex(1);\n\n        // Get all options\n        List<WebElement> allOptions = dropdown.getOptions();\n        System.out.println(\"Total options: \" + allOptions.size());\n        for (WebElement opt : allOptions) {\n            System.out.println(\" - \" + opt.getText() + \" (value=\" + opt.getAttribute(\"value\") + \")\");\n        }\n\n        // --- Multi-select example ---\n        // driver.get(\"https://example.com/multi-select\");\n        // WebElement multi = driver.findElement(By.id(\"multiSelect\"));\n        // Select multiSelect = new Select(multi);\n        // if (multiSelect.isMultiple()) {\n        //     multiSelect.selectByVisibleText(\"Java\");\n        //     multiSelect.selectByVisibleText(\"Python\");\n        //     System.out.println(\"Selected count: \" + multiSelect.getAllSelectedOptions().size());\n        //     multiSelect.deselectAll();\n        // }\n\n        // --- Custom (non-select) Dropdown ---\n        // For React-Select type dropdowns:\n        // driver.findElement(By.cssSelector(\"div.select__control\")).click();\n        // driver.findElement(By.xpath(\"//div[text()='Option 2']\")).click();\n\n        driver.quit();\n    }\n}","steps":[{"title":"Select Wrapper","lines":"14-16","desc":"Select class wraps &lt;select&gt; WebElement and provides high-level methods. It validates tagName is 'select' else throws UnexpectedTagNameException — early failure for custom dropdowns."},{"title":"Three Selection Strategies","lines":"18-27","desc":"VisibleText matches displayed text (trimmed). Value matches value attribute — more stable than text. Index is position (0-based) — brittle, avoid unless no value/text."},{"title":"Introspection","lines":"29-34","desc":"getOptions() returns List&lt;WebElement&gt; of &lt;option&gt;. getFirstSelectedOption() for single-select current value. isMultiple() distinguishes single vs multi — crucial before deselect."},{"title":"Multi-select Workflow","lines":"36-46","desc":"Only if isMultiple true, you can select multiple. getAllSelectedOptions() returns selected ones. deselectAll() clears. Single-select will throw on deselect methods."},{"title":"Custom Dropdown Fallback","lines":"48-51","desc":"For div-based dropdowns, click control to open, wait for options visible, click by text. No Select class. Use explicit wait (Module 9) for options after click."}],"snip":["Select country = new Select(driver.findElement(By.id(\"country\")));\ncountry.selectByVisibleText(\"India\");\ncountry.selectByValue(\"IN\");\ncountry.selectByIndex(2);\nfor (WebElement o : country.getOptions()) System.out.println(o.getText());\nSystem.out.println(country.getFirstSelectedOption().getText());\n\nSelect skills = new Select(driver.findElement(By.id(\"skills\")));\nif (skills.isMultiple()) { skills.selectByIndex(0); skills.selectByIndex(2); skills.deselectAll(); }\n\n// custom dropdown\ndriver.findElement(By.id(\"city\")).click();\ndriver.findElement(By.xpath(\"//ul[@id='list']/li[text()='Chennai']\")).click();"],"best":["Prefer selectByValue over visibleText — value is less likely to change due to i18n.","Wrap Select in Page Object method: selectCountry(String country) hides locator.","For custom dropdowns, create helper that clicks and waits for option list — reusable."],"bad":["Using Select on div-based dropdown — throws UnexpectedTagNameException. Inspect HTML first.","selectByIndex(0) selecting placeholder 'Please select' — validate with getFirstSelectedOption().getText().","Not checking isMultiple before deselectAll — throws UnsupportedOperationException on single-select.","<code>NoSuchElementException</code> from <code>selectByVisibleText</code> usually means extra spaces or case mismatch in the text.","Interview: validate dropdown options are sorted by copying <code>getOptions()</code> texts into a list and comparing with a sorted copy."],"sim":["[Select] isMultiple: false","[Select] selectByVisibleText: Option 1 -> SELECTED","Selected: Option 1","[Select] selectByValue: 2 -> SELECTED Option 2","[Select] selectByIndex: 1 -> Option 1","Total options: 3"," - Please select an option (value=)"," - Option 1 (value=1)"," - Option 2 (value=2)","[Custom] React-Select: click control, wait options, click text"]},{"t":"Wait Mechanisms","s":"Implicit wait, explicit wait and fluent wait.","est":"45 min","lvl":"Intermediate","an":["Shops open slowly. Selly could <b>wait N minutes at every door</b> (implicit), <b>wait for this particular shop to open</b> (explicit), or <b>check every 500 ms and ignore \"not ready yet\" notices</b> (fluent)."],"why":["<b>What:</b> waits synchronise your script with the page. <b>Why:</b> modern pages load data via AJAX; Selenium is faster than the page, so without waits tests fail randomly (flaky tests), which wastes team time and destroys trust in automation."],"obj":["Understand implicit, explicit, fluent waits","Use WebDriverWait with ExpectedConditions","Implement FluentWait with polling and ignored exceptions","Avoid Thread.sleep and mixed waits"],"theory":["Web is async — Selenium executes faster than page renders. Without waits, NoSuchElementException. Implicit wait: driver.manage().timeouts().implicitlyWait(10 sec) — global, waits for element to appear on every findElement. But it applies to findElements too (waits full timeout if 0). And it doesn't wait for visibility/clickability, just presence in DOM.","Explicit wait: WebDriverWait + ExpectedConditions — waits for specific condition (elementToBeClickable, visibilityOf, etc) with timeout. Most flexible, recommended. Example: new WebDriverWait(driver, Duration.ofSeconds(10)).until(ExpectedConditions.elementToBeClickable(By.id('submit'))). It polls every 500ms by default.","FluentWait is parent of WebDriverWait, allows custom polling interval and ignored exceptions: withTimeout, pollingEvery, ignoring(NoSuchElementException.class). Use for elements that appear/disappear frequently or for custom conditions. Never mix implicit and explicit — causes unpredictable 10s+10s = 20s wait. Set implicit to 0 and use explicit only."],"pts":["<b>Implicit:</b> set once; applies to every <code>findElement</code>; polls the DOM until the element exists or time runs out. Does not wait for clickability or text.","<b>Explicit:</b> <code>WebDriverWait</code> plus <code>ExpectedConditions</code>: <code>visibilityOfElementLocated</code>, <code>elementToBeClickable</code>, <code>presenceOfElementLocated</code>, <code>titleContains</code>, <code>alertIsPresent</code>, <code>invisibilityOfElementLocated</code>.","<b>Fluent:</b> an explicit wait with custom <code>pollingEvery</code> and <code>ignoring(Exception)</code>.","<b>Page load timeout:</b> <code>manage().timeouts().pageLoadTimeout(...)</code>.","<b>Avoid</b> <code>Thread.sleep()</code>: it always waits the full time.","Do not mix implicit and explicit waits; the combined timeout becomes unpredictable."],"file":"WaitDemo.java","path":"module09/WaitDemo.java","code":"package com.seleniumlearning.module09;\n\nimport org.openqa.selenium.*;\nimport org.openqa.selenium.chrome.ChromeDriver;\nimport org.openqa.selenium.support.ui.ExpectedConditions;\nimport org.openqa.selenium.support.ui.FluentWait;\nimport org.openqa.selenium.support.ui.WebDriverWait;\nimport io.github.bonigarcia.wdm.WebDriverManager;\nimport java.time.Duration;\nimport java.util.function.Function;\n\npublic class WaitDemo {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        WebDriverManager.chromedriver().setup();\n        WebDriver driver = new ChromeDriver();\n        driver.manage().timeouts().implicitlyWait(Duration.ofSeconds(0)); // Best practice: 0\n\n        driver.get(\"https://the-internet.herokuapp.com/dynamic_loading/1\");\n\n        // --- Explicit Wait (Recommended) ---\n        WebDriverWait wait = new WebDriverWait(driver, Duration.ofSeconds(10));\n        WebElement startBtn = driver.findElement(By.cssSelector(\"#start button\"));\n        startBtn.click();\n\n        // Wait for element to be visible\n        WebElement finishText = wait.until(\n            ExpectedConditions.visibilityOfElementLocated(By.id(\"finish\"))\n        );\n        System.out.println(\"Loaded text: \" + finishText.getText());\n\n        // Other ExpectedConditions:\n        // wait.until(ExpectedConditions.elementToBeClickable(By.id(\"submit\")));\n        // wait.until(ExpectedConditions.titleContains(\"Dashboard\"));\n        // wait.until(ExpectedConditions.urlContains(\"/dashboard\"));\n        // wait.until(ExpectedConditions.alertIsPresent());\n\n        // --- Custom ExpectedCondition (lambda) ---\n        WebElement customWait = wait.until(driver1 -> {\n            WebElement el = driver1.findElement(By.id(\"finish\"));\n            return el.isDisplayed() ? el : null;\n        });\n\n        // --- FluentWait (advanced polling) ---\n        FluentWait<WebDriver> fluentWait = new FluentWait<>(driver)\n                .withTimeout(Duration.ofSeconds(15))\n                .pollingEvery(Duration.ofMillis(500))\n                .ignoring(NoSuchElementException.class)\n                .ignoring(StaleElementReferenceException.class);\n\n        // fluentWait.until((Function<WebDriver, WebElement>) d ->\n        //     d.findElement(By.id(\"finish\")));\n\n        System.out.println(\"FluentWait configured: 15s timeout, 500ms polling\");\n\n        driver.quit();\n    }\n}","steps":[{"title":"Zero Implicit Wait","lines":"13-14","desc":"Setting implicit to 0 disables global wait. This prevents explicit waits from being multiplied. Modern best practice: never use implicit, use explicit for each interaction needing wait."},{"title":"Explicit Wait Core","lines":"17-25","desc":"WebDriverWait polls every 500ms until condition met or timeout. ExpectedConditions provides 30+ conditions: visibility, clickability, presence, text. Returns WebElement so you can chain .click() directly."},{"title":"Common Conditions","lines":"27-31","desc":"elementToBeClickable checks visible + enabled. titleContains/urlContains for navigation. alertIsPresent for alerts. invisibilityOf for spinners disappearing. Choose precise condition, not just presence."},{"title":"Custom Lambda Condition","lines":"33-37","desc":"wait.until(driver -&gt; {...}) lets you write custom logic returning element or boolean. Return null/false to keep polling. Useful for complex checks like table row count &gt; 5."},{"title":"FluentWait Control","lines":"40-49","desc":"FluentWait lets you set polling interval (e.g., 100ms for fast UI) and ignore specific exceptions like NoSuchElement and StaleElement. Essential for highly dynamic AJAX apps."}],"snip":["driver.manage().timeouts().implicitlyWait(Duration.ofSeconds(10));\n\nWebDriverWait wait = new WebDriverWait(driver, Duration.ofSeconds(15));\nWebElement pay = wait.until(ExpectedConditions.elementToBeClickable(By.id(\"pay\")));\npay.click();\n\nWait<WebDriver> fluent = new FluentWait<>(driver)\n    .withTimeout(Duration.ofSeconds(30))\n    .pollingEvery(Duration.ofMillis(500))\n    .ignoring(NoSuchElementException.class);\nWebElement msg = fluent.until(d -> d.findElement(By.id(\"done\")));"],"best":["Use explicit wait for every interaction that triggers async: click that loads data, navigation, etc.","Create WaitUtils class with methods waitForClickable(By, int seconds) to avoid repeating WebDriverWait.","Never use Thread.sleep — it waits full time even if element ready in 100ms, making suite slow. Explicit returns immediately when ready."],"bad":["Mixing implicit 10s + explicit 10s: findElement waits 10s implicitly, then explicit waits another 10s = 20s delay.","Using presenceOfElementLocated when you need visibility — element may be in DOM but hidden, click fails.","Catching TimeoutException and continuing — should fail test. Timeout means app not in expected state.","Interview favourite: implicit vs explicit vs fluent. Answer: scope (global vs per element), conditions supported, and polling control.","<code>TimeoutException</code> means the condition never became true; check the locator or the condition."],"sim":["[Config] implicitWait = 0s (explicit only)","[Action] click() #start button -> triggers loading","[Explicit] Waiting for visibilityOf #finish, timeout 10s, polling 500ms","[Poll 500ms] #finish not visible","[Poll 1000ms] #finish not visible","[Poll 3500ms] #finish visible -> FOUND","Loaded text: Hello World!","[Fluent] Config: timeout 15s, polling 500ms, ignoring NoSuch, Stale","[Result] Custom condition passed, element displayed"]},{"t":"Alerts, Frames, Windows","s":"JavaScript alerts, frame handling and window handles.","est":"45 min","lvl":"Intermediate","an":["An <b>announcement speaker</b> blocks everything until Selly responds (alert). Some shops are <b>shops inside shops</b> (frames); she must step inside before she can see its items. Sometimes a click opens a <b>new mall branch</b> (new window or tab) and she must say which branch she is working in."],"why":["<b>Why:</b> payment gateways, ads, rich-text editors and \"open in new tab\" links all appear in real apps. Selenium only sees one context at a time, so without switching you get <code>NoSuchElementException</code> for elements that are plainly on screen."],"obj":["Handle JavaScript alerts, confirms, prompts","Switch between frames and nested frames","Manage multiple windows/tabs with handles","Return to default content correctly"],"theory":["JavaScript alerts are modal dialogs: alert (OK only), confirm (OK/Cancel), prompt (input). Selenium blocks until alert handled. switchTo().alert() returns Alert interface: accept() (OK), dismiss() (Cancel), getText(), sendKeys() for prompt. Always use explicit wait alertIsPresent() before switching — alert may take time to appear.","Frames are &lt;iframe&gt; or &lt;frame&gt; — separate DOM. Driver context is main page by default, cannot see inside frame. switchTo().frame() by index (0), name/id, or WebElement. After switching, findElement searches inside frame only. To go back: parentFrame() (one level up) or defaultContent() (main page). Nested frames require sequential switches: switch to parent frame, then child.","Windows/tabs: each has unique handle (GUID). getWindowHandle() returns current, getWindowHandles() returns Set&lt;String&gt; of all. To switch: iterate handles, switchTo().window(handle). For new tab opened via click, wait for number of handles to be 2, then switch. Always store parent handle before opening new window to return."],"pts":["<b>Alert:</b> <code>driver.switchTo().alert()</code> gives <code>accept()</code>, <code>dismiss()</code>, <code>getText()</code>, <code>sendKeys()</code> (prompt). Types: simple, confirm, prompt. HTML popups are normal elements, not alerts.","<b>Frames:</b> <code>switchTo().frame(index | \"nameOrId\" | WebElement)</code>; <code>parentFrame()</code> goes up one level; <code>defaultContent()</code> returns to the page. For nested frames switch step by step.","<b>Windows:</b> <code>getWindowHandle()</code> is the current one; <code>getWindowHandles()</code> returns a <code>Set&lt;String&gt;</code>; <code>switchTo().window(handle)</code> moves.","<b>Selenium 4:</b> <code>switchTo().newWindow(WindowType.TAB)</code>."],"file":"AlertsFramesWindowsDemo.java","path":"module10/AlertsFramesWindowsDemo.java","code":"package com.seleniumlearning.module10;\n\nimport org.openqa.selenium.*;\nimport org.openqa.selenium.chrome.ChromeDriver;\nimport org.openqa.selenium.support.ui.ExpectedConditions;\nimport org.openqa.selenium.support.ui.WebDriverWait;\nimport io.github.bonigarcia.wdm.WebDriverManager;\nimport java.time.Duration;\nimport java.util.Set;\n\npublic class AlertsFramesWindowsDemo {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        WebDriverManager.chromedriver().setup();\n        WebDriver driver = new ChromeDriver();\n        driver.get(\"https://the-internet.herokuapp.com/javascript_alerts\");\n\n        WebDriverWait wait = new WebDriverWait(driver, Duration.ofSeconds(10));\n\n        // --- Alerts ---\n        driver.findElement(By.xpath(\"//button[text()='Click for JS Alert']\")).click();\n        Alert alert = wait.until(ExpectedConditions.alertIsPresent());\n        System.out.println(\"Alert text: \" + alert.getText());\n        alert.accept(); // Click OK\n\n        // Confirm Alert\n        driver.findElement(By.xpath(\"//button[text()='Click for JS Confirm']\")).click();\n        Alert confirm = wait.until(ExpectedConditions.alertIsPresent());\n        System.out.println(\"Confirm text: \" + confirm.getText());\n        confirm.dismiss(); // Click Cancel\n\n        // Prompt Alert\n        driver.findElement(By.xpath(\"//button[text()='Click for JS Prompt']\")).click();\n        Alert prompt = wait.until(ExpectedConditions.alertIsPresent());\n        prompt.sendKeys(\"Selenium Test\");\n        prompt.accept();\n\n        // --- Frames ---\n        driver.get(\"https://the-internet.herokuapp.com/iframe\");\n        // Switch to frame by WebElement\n        WebElement frameElement = driver.findElement(By.id(\"mce_0_ifr\"));\n        driver.switchTo().frame(frameElement);\n\n        WebElement editor = driver.findElement(By.id(\"tinymce\"));\n        editor.clear();\n        editor.sendKeys(\"Hello from inside frame!\");\n\n        driver.switchTo().defaultContent(); // Back to main page\n        System.out.println(\"Back to main page, header: \" +\n            driver.findElement(By.tagName(\"h3\")).getText());\n\n        // --- Windows ---\n        driver.get(\"https://the-internet.herokuapp.com/windows\");\n        String parentHandle = driver.getWindowHandle();\n        System.out.println(\"Parent handle: \" + parentHandle);\n\n        driver.findElement(By.linkText(\"Click Here\")).click();\n\n        // Wait for new window\n        wait.until(d -> d.getWindowHandles().size() > 1);\n        Set<String> allHandles = driver.getWindowHandles();\n\n        for (String handle : allHandles) {\n            if (!handle.equals(parentHandle)) {\n                driver.switchTo().window(handle);\n                System.out.println(\"Child window title: \" + driver.getTitle());\n                System.out.println(\"Child text: \" + driver.findElement(By.tagName(\"h3\")).getText());\n                driver.close(); // Close child\n            }\n        }\n\n        driver.switchTo().window(parentHandle);\n        System.out.println(\"Back to parent: \" + driver.getTitle());\n        driver.quit();\n    }\n}","steps":[{"title":"Alert Handling Pattern","lines":"14-21","desc":"Click triggers alert. Explicit wait alertIsPresent() prevents NoAlertPresentException. getText() reads message for assertion. accept() = OK, dismiss() = Cancel. Always handle, else next command throws UnhandledAlertException."},{"title":"Prompt with Input","lines":"29-33","desc":"For prompt dialogs, sendKeys() types into prompt before accept(). This is only place sendKeys works on Alert, not WebElement."},{"title":"Frame Switching","lines":"36-46","desc":"Switch by WebElement is most stable (not index). After switch, driver context is inside iframe — main page elements not accessible. Must defaultContent() to return. For nested frames, chain switches."},{"title":"Window Handle Management","lines":"49-60","desc":"Store parent handle before opening new window. After click, wait for handles size &gt;1 (explicit). Loop through handles, switch to child that is not parent. close() child, then switch back to parent."},{"title":"Context Return","lines":"62-68","desc":"After child close, switch to parent handle else NoSuchWindowException. defaultContent() is for frames, window() for windows — don't confuse. Both reset context."}],"snip":["// Alert\ndriver.findElement(By.id(\"delete\")).click();\nAlert a = new WebDriverWait(driver, Duration.ofSeconds(5)).until(ExpectedConditions.alertIsPresent());\nSystem.out.println(a.getText());\na.accept();\n\n// Frame\ndriver.switchTo().frame(\"payFrame\");\ndriver.findElement(By.id(\"card\")).sendKeys(\"4111111111111111\");\ndriver.switchTo().defaultContent();\n\n// Windows\nString parent = driver.getWindowHandle();\ndriver.findElement(By.linkText(\"Terms\")).click();\nfor (String h : driver.getWindowHandles())\n  if (!h.equals(parent)) { driver.switchTo().window(h); break; }\ndriver.close();\ndriver.switchTo().window(parent);"],"best":["Always wait for alertIsPresent() — alerts are async, may take 500ms to appear after click.","For frames, create Page Object that switches in constructor and switches back in method — encapsulates context.","Use ArrayList of handles for ordered access: new ArrayList&lt;&gt;(driver.getWindowHandles()).get(1) for second window."],"bad":["Calling switchTo().alert() without wait — NoAlertPresentException if alert delayed.","Forgetting defaultContent() after frame operation — next findElement fails because still inside frame.","Not storing parent handle — loses reference after opening multiple windows, cannot return.","Always switch back to the parent window after <code>close()</code>; otherwise <code>NoSuchWindowException</code>.","<code>UnhandledAlertException</code> appears when an alert is open and you try another command."],"sim":["[Click] JS Alert button","[Explicit] alertIsPresent() -> FOUND","Alert text: I am a JS Alert","[Alert] accept()","[Click] JS Confirm","Confirm text: I am a JS Confirm","[Alert] dismiss() -> Cancel","[Frame] switchTo frame id=mce_0_ifr","[Frame] clear + sendKeys 'Hello from inside frame!'","[Frame] defaultContent()","Back to main page, header: An iFrame containing the TinyMCE WYSIWYG Editor","[Window] parent handle: CDwindow-123","[Click] Click Here -> new window","[Window] child title: New Window, text: New Window","[Window] close child, switch back to parent"]},{"t":"Advanced User Interactions","s":"Actions class, mouse and keyboard events, drag and drop.","est":"50 min","lvl":"Advanced","an":["Some deliveries need <b>complex moves</b>: hover over a display so a drawer slides out (mouse hover), double-tap a button, right-click a menu, drag a trolley to the loading bay (drag and drop), or hold Shift while pressing keys."],"why":["<b>What:</b> the <code>Actions</code> class builds a chain of low-level input events. <b>Why:</b> menus that open on hover, sliders, canvas boards, kanban drag-and-drop and keyboard shortcuts cannot be done with plain <code>click()</code>."],"obj":["Use Actions class for complex mouse/keyboard","Implement hover, double-click, right-click, drag-drop","Handle sliders, resizable, sortable","Perform keyboard shortcuts and combos"],"theory":["Actions class chains low-level interactions: moveToElement (hover), doubleClick, contextClick (right-click), dragAndDrop, clickAndHold, moveByOffset, keyDown/keyUp. Build pattern: new Actions(driver).moveToElement(menu).click(submenu).build().perform(). build() compiles actions, perform() executes. Without build().perform(), nothing happens.","Hover reveals hidden menus — moveToElement triggers mouseover event. For dropdown menus, hover parent, wait for child visible, then click child. Drag and drop: dragAndDrop(source, target) or clickAndHold(source).moveToElement(target).release(). For sliders, dragAndDropBy with xOffset.","Keyboard: keyDown(Keys.CONTROL).sendKeys('a').keyUp(Keys.CONTROL) for select all. sendKeys(Keys.ENTER, Keys.TAB) etc. For OS-level dialogs (file upload), sendKeys to &lt;input type='file'&gt; is better than Actions. Actions sends to browser, not OS."],"pts":["Create: <code>Actions act = new Actions(driver);</code> then chain and finish with <code>.build().perform()</code> (or just <code>.perform()</code>).","<b>Mouse:</b> <code>moveToElement</code>, <code>click</code>, <code>doubleClick</code>, <code>contextClick</code>, <code>clickAndHold</code>, <code>release</code>, <code>dragAndDrop(src,target)</code>, <code>dragAndDropBy(el,x,y)</code>, <code>moveByOffset</code>.","<b>Keyboard:</b> <code>sendKeys</code>, <code>keyDown(Keys.SHIFT)</code>, <code>keyUp(...)</code>; Ctrl+A / Ctrl+C using <code>Keys.CONTROL</code>.","<b>Selenium 4:</b> <code>scrollToElement</code>, <code>scrollByAmount</code>."],"file":"AdvancedActionsDemo.java","path":"module11/AdvancedActionsDemo.java","code":"package com.seleniumlearning.module11;\n\nimport org.openqa.selenium.By;\nimport org.openqa.selenium.Keys;\nimport org.openqa.selenium.WebDriver;\nimport org.openqa.selenium.WebElement;\nimport org.openqa.selenium.chrome.ChromeDriver;\nimport org.openqa.selenium.interactions.Actions;\nimport io.github.bonigarcia.wdm.WebDriverManager;\n\npublic class AdvancedActionsDemo {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        WebDriverManager.chromedriver().setup();\n        WebDriver driver = new ChromeDriver();\n        Actions actions = new Actions(driver);\n\n        driver.get(\"https://the-internet.herokuapp.com/hovers\");\n\n        // --- Hover (moveToElement) ---\n        WebElement avatar = driver.findElement(By.cssSelector(\".figure:nth-child(1)\"));\n        actions.moveToElement(avatar).perform();\n        WebElement caption = driver.findElement(By.cssSelector(\".figure:nth-child(1) .figcaption\"));\n        System.out.println(\"Hover caption visible: \" + caption.isDisplayed());\n        System.out.println(\"Caption text: \" + caption.getText());\n\n        // --- Double Click ---\n        driver.get(\"https://api.jquery.com/dblclick/\");\n        driver.switchTo().frame(0);\n        WebElement dblBox = driver.findElement(By.cssSelector(\"div\"));\n        actions.doubleClick(dblBox).perform();\n        System.out.println(\"Double clicked\");\n\n        // --- Right Click (Context Click) ---\n        driver.get(\"https://the-internet.herokuapp.com/context_menu\");\n        WebElement hotSpot = driver.findElement(By.id(\"hot-spot\"));\n        actions.contextClick(hotSpot).perform();\n        driver.switchTo().alert().accept();\n\n        // --- Drag and Drop ---\n        driver.get(\"https://the-internet.herokuapp.com/drag_and_drop\");\n        WebElement source = driver.findElement(By.id(\"column-a\"));\n        WebElement target = driver.findElement(By.id(\"column-b\"));\n        actions.dragAndDrop(source, target).perform();\n        System.out.println(\"Dragged A to B\");\n\n        // --- Slider Drag by Offset ---\n        // WebElement slider = driver.findElement(By.cssSelector(\"input[type='range']\"));\n        // actions.clickAndHold(slider).moveByOffset(50, 0).release().perform();\n\n        // --- Keyboard Actions ---\n        driver.get(\"https://the-internet.herokuapp.com/key_presses\");\n        WebElement input = driver.findElement(By.id(\"target\"));\n        input.click();\n        actions.keyDown(Keys.SHIFT).sendKeys(\"a\").keyUp(Keys.SHIFT).perform();\n        // Sends 'A' (shift + a)\n\n        actions.keyDown(Keys.CONTROL).sendKeys(\"a\").keyUp(Keys.CONTROL).perform();\n        actions.sendKeys(Keys.DELETE).perform();\n\n        driver.quit();\n    }\n}","steps":[{"title":"Actions Initialization","lines":"11-12","desc":"Actions requires WebDriver instance. It builds internal action sequence. Each method returns Actions for chaining. Must call perform() at end — otherwise actions queued but not executed."},{"title":"Hover for Hidden Elements","lines":"15-20","desc":"moveToElement triggers mouseover, which via CSS :hover shows hidden caption. Need to wait after hover for visibility. Common for mega menus: hover parent, then click child that appears."},{"title":"Double &amp; Context Click","lines":"23-33","desc":"doubleClick triggers dblclick event. contextClick triggers contextmenu event (right-click). Both may open custom menus. For browser default context menu, you can't interact — need to handle custom div menu that appears after."},{"title":"Drag and Drop","lines":"36-43","desc":"dragAndDrop uses HTML5 DnD API. Some apps use custom JS DnD that Selenium's method doesn't trigger — fallback to clickAndHold, moveByOffset, release sequence. Add pause(Duration) for visual debugging."},{"title":"Keyboard Combos","lines":"49-57","desc":"keyDown holds key, keyUp releases. Must release else key stays pressed for next actions. SHIFT+a = A. CONTROL+a = select all. Use Keys.chord for simpler combo: Keys.chord(Keys.CONTROL, 'a')."}],"snip":["Actions act = new Actions(driver);\nact.moveToElement(driver.findElement(By.id(\"menu\"))).perform();\ndriver.findElement(By.linkText(\"Sub item\")).click();\n\nact.doubleClick(driver.findElement(By.id(\"dbl\"))).perform();\nact.contextClick(driver.findElement(By.id(\"area\"))).perform();\n\nWebElement src = driver.findElement(By.id(\"drag\"));\nWebElement dst = driver.findElement(By.id(\"drop\"));\nact.dragAndDrop(src, dst).perform();\n// fallback if dragAndDrop fails\nact.clickAndHold(src).moveToElement(dst).release().perform();\n\nact.keyDown(Keys.CONTROL).sendKeys(\"a\").keyUp(Keys.CONTROL).perform();"],"best":["Chain actions: moveToElement(menu).pause(500ms).moveToElement(submenu).click().build().perform() — pause ensures submenu rendered.","For HTML5 drag-drop failures, use JSExecutor helper that dispatches drag events — more reliable than Actions in some frameworks.","Always release held keys/mouse in finally or after test — stuck keys cause next test to fail mysteriously."],"bad":["Forgetting perform() — code runs no error but no action happens. Most common Actions mistake.","moveToElement on element not in viewport — throws MoveTargetOutOfBoundsException. Scroll into view first.","Using dragAndDrop on canvas elements — may need offset-based drag. Use dragAndDropBy or moveByOffset.","Forgetting <code>perform()</code> is the classic bug: nothing happens.","HTML5 drag-and-drop sometimes needs JavaScript; see the next module."],"sim":["[Actions] moveToElement .figure:nth-child(1) -> perform","Hover caption visible: true","Caption text: name: user1 View profile","[Actions] doubleClick div -> perform","Double clicked, color changed","[Actions] contextClick #hot-spot -> alert","[Alert] accept() context menu alert","[Actions] dragAndDrop #column-a -> #column-b -> perform","Dragged A to B, columns swapped","[Actions] keyDown SHIFT, sendKeys a, keyUp SHIFT -> 'A'","[Actions] Ctrl+A + Delete -> input cleared"]},{"t":"JavaScriptExecutor","s":"Scroll, click via JS, handling hidden elements.","est":"40 min","lvl":"Advanced","an":["When the normal route is blocked (a banner covers the door, or the shop is hidden), Selly uses the <b>staff-only service lift</b>: she talks directly to the mall's control panel (the browser's JavaScript engine) and says \"scroll there\" or \"press that button for me\"."],"why":["<b>Why:</b> some actions have no Selenium method, or the element is covered or hidden (<code>ElementClickInterceptedException</code>, read-only date pickers, lazy-loaded pages). JS lets you work around them, mostly as a last resort."],"obj":["Execute JavaScript for edge cases","Scroll, click via JS, handle hidden elements","Highlight elements and get page info via JS","Understand executeScript vs executeAsyncScript"],"theory":["JavaScriptExecutor is interface that WebDriver implements: (JavascriptExecutor)driver.executeScript(). Lets you run JS in browser context. Use cases: click when WebDriver click blocked by overlay, scrollIntoView for infinite scroll, get page title via return document.title, highlight element with style border, set value of hidden input.","executeScript is synchronous — returns immediately after JS executed. First arg is JS string, following args are arguments[0], arguments[1] etc that map to Java objects (WebElement, String). Return types converted: WebElement, Long, String, Boolean, List. For scrolling: arguments[0].scrollIntoView(true). For click: arguments[0].click().","executeAsyncScript is async — last argument is callback function that JS must call to signal completion. Use for waiting for async operations in JS. For most Selenium tasks, executeScript is enough. Scroll methods: window.scrollBy(0,500), window.scrollTo(0, document.body.scrollHeight) for bottom, element.scrollIntoView()."],"pts":["Cast: <code>JavascriptExecutor js = (JavascriptExecutor) driver;</code>.","<code>js.executeScript(\"script\", args)</code>; elements are passed as <code>arguments[0]</code>; the return value is available.","<b>Scroll:</b> <code>window.scrollBy(0,500)</code>, <code>window.scrollTo(0,document.body.scrollHeight)</code>, <code>arguments[0].scrollIntoView(true)</code>.","<b>Click:</b> <code>arguments[0].click()</code> ignores overlays.","<b>Set value:</b> <code>arguments[0].value='2025-01-31'</code> for read-only date inputs.","Also: read <code>document.title</code>, <code>document.readyState</code>, highlight elements by changing <code>style.border</code>."],"file":"JSDemo.java","path":"module12/JSDemo.java","code":"package com.seleniumlearning.module12;\n\nimport org.openqa.selenium.*;\nimport org.openqa.selenium.chrome.ChromeDriver;\nimport io.github.bonigarcia.wdm.WebDriverManager;\n\npublic class JSDemo {\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws InterruptedException {\n        WebDriverManager.chromedriver().setup();\n        WebDriver driver = new ChromeDriver();\n        JavascriptExecutor js = (JavascriptExecutor) driver;\n\n        driver.get(\"https://the-internet.herokuapp.com/large\");\n\n        // --- Scrolling ---\n        // Scroll by pixels\n        js.executeScript(\"window.scrollBy(0, 500)\");\n        Thread.sleep(500);\n\n        // Scroll to bottom\n        js.executeScript(\"window.scrollTo(0, document.body.scrollHeight)\");\n        Thread.sleep(500);\n\n        // Scroll into view specific element\n        WebElement table = driver.findElement(By.id(\"large-table\"));\n        js.executeScript(\"arguments[0].scrollIntoView({behavior: 'smooth', block: 'center'});\", table);\n\n        // --- Click via JS (when normal click fails) ---\n        WebElement link = driver.findElement(By.linkText(\"Elemental Selenium\"));\n        js.executeScript(\"arguments[0].click();\", link);\n\n        // --- Highlight element for debugging ---\n        WebElement header = driver.findElement(By.tagName(\"h3\"));\n        js.executeScript(\"arguments[0].style.border='3px solid red'; arguments[0].style.background='yellow';\", header);\n        Thread.sleep(1000);\n        js.executeScript(\"arguments[0].style.border=''; arguments[0].style.background='';\", header);\n\n        // --- Get info via JS ---\n        String title = (String) js.executeScript(\"return document.title;\");\n        Long innerWidth = (Long) js.executeScript(\"return window.innerWidth;\");\n        System.out.println(\"Title via JS: \" + title);\n        System.out.println(\"Inner width: \" + innerWidth);\n\n        // --- Handle hidden element ---\n        // For <input type='hidden' id='hiddenField'>\n        // js.executeScript(\"document.getElementById('hiddenField').value='secret';\");\n\n        // --- Return WebElement from JS ---\n        WebElement body = (WebElement) js.executeScript(\"return document.body;\");\n        System.out.println(\"Body tag: \" + body.getTagName());\n\n        driver.quit();\n    }\n}","steps":[{"title":"Casting to JSExecutor","lines":"9-10","desc":"ChromeDriver implements JavascriptExecutor, so cast. All drivers do. Create js variable once and reuse. executeScript takes JS string + varargs for arguments."},{"title":"Scrolling Strategies","lines":"13-23","desc":"scrollBy for relative, scrollTo for absolute, scrollIntoView for element. Smooth behavior for visual. For infinite scroll, loop scrollTo bottom + wait for new content count increase."},{"title":"JS Click Workaround","lines":"25-27","desc":"When WebDriver click fails with 'ElementClickIntercepted' due to overlay, JS click bypasses overlay check — clicks directly in DOM. But it doesn't trigger hover or real user events, so use only as fallback."},{"title":"Highlight for Debugging","lines":"29-34","desc":"Temporarily add border/background to visualize element found. Useful in screenshots. Remove after to avoid affecting next steps. Can be utility method highlightElement(WebElement)."},{"title":"Return Values","lines":"36-48","desc":"JS return values converted: String, Long, Boolean, WebElement, List. document.title, window.innerWidth, document.body are quick checks. For hidden inputs, set value via JS directly."}],"snip":["JavascriptExecutor js = (JavascriptExecutor) driver;\nWebElement footer = driver.findElement(By.id(\"footer\"));\njs.executeScript(\"arguments[0].scrollIntoView(true);\", footer);\njs.executeScript(\"window.scrollTo(0, document.body.scrollHeight)\");\n\nWebElement hidden = driver.findElement(By.id(\"hiddenBtn\"));\njs.executeScript(\"arguments[0].click();\", hidden);\n\nWebElement date = driver.findElement(By.id(\"dob\"));\njs.executeScript(\"arguments[0].value='1995-08-15';\", date);\n\nString state = (String) js.executeScript(\"return document.readyState\");"],"best":["Create JSUtils class: scrollIntoView, clickViaJS, highlight, getInnerText — reuse everywhere.","Use JS click only when WebDriver click fails after trying scroll and explicit wait — JS click doesn't mimic user, may miss bugs.","For shadow DOM, JSExecutor is only way: return arguments[0].shadowRoot.querySelector('button') — WebDriver can't pierce shadow root directly in Selenium 3 (Selenium 4 has getShadowRoot)."],"bad":["executeScript('document.getElementById(\"id\").click()') — hardcoding ID in string instead of using arguments[0] — breaks when ID dynamic.","Not casting driver to JavascriptExecutor — compile error. Remember cast.","Using JS to set value of visible input without triggering change events — React state not updated. Use sendKeys or dispatch events via JS.","JS click bypasses real-user checks, so it can hide genuine UI bugs. Prefer normal <code>click()</code> first.","Interview: when would you use JavascriptExecutor? Hidden/covered elements, scrolling, setting values, and page info."],"sim":["[JS] window.scrollBy(0, 500)","[JS] window.scrollTo(0, document.body.scrollHeight) -> bottom","[JS] arguments[0].scrollIntoView smooth center -> large-table","[JS] arguments[0].click() Elemental Selenium","[JS] Highlight h3 with red border + yellow bg","[JS] return document.title -> 'Large & Deep DOM'","Title via JS: Large & Deep DOM","Inner width: 1920","[JS] return document.body -> WebElement","Body tag: body"]},{"t":"Handling Web Tables","s":"Static and dynamic tables, row and column traversal.","est":"45 min","lvl":"Advanced","an":["The mall's <b>notice board</b> lists every shop in rows and columns. Selly reads it by rows (one shop), by columns (all prices), or finds one shop by name and reads the cell next to it. If the board grows during the day, that is a <b>dynamic table</b>."],"why":["<b>Why:</b> orders, users, invoices and reports are shown in tables. Tests must verify counts, totals, sorting and row-specific actions such as \"click Edit on the row where Name is Ravi\"."],"obj":["Traverse static and dynamic tables","Extract rows, columns, specific cells","Handle pagination and dynamic search in tables","Perform calculations on table data"],"theory":["Tables: &lt;table&gt;&lt;thead&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;th&gt;..&lt;/th&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/thead&gt;&lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;..&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt;. Static tables have fixed rows. Dynamic tables load via AJAX, rows may change. To handle: find table element, then findElements(By.tagName('tr')) for rows, then for each row findElements(By.tagName('td')) for cells. thead vs tbody separation matters.","Row/column traversal: //table[@id='customers']/tbody/tr for all rows, //table/tbody/tr[2] second row, //table/tbody/tr[2]/td[3] second row third column. For dynamic search: iterate rows, check if row text contains target, then act on that row's button.","Pagination: tables with Next button — loop while Next enabled, search current page, if not found click Next and wait for table reload (staleness). Dynamic tables may have sorting — click header to sort, then verify sorted order. For calculations: extract price column, parse to double, sum."],"pts":["Structure: <code>table &gt; thead/tbody &gt; tr &gt; th/td</code>.","<b>Static:</b> fixed XPath such as <code>//table[@id='t']/tbody/tr[2]/td[3]</code>.","<b>Dynamic:</b> count rows with <code>findElements(By.xpath(\"//table[@id='t']//tr\"))</code> and loop; never hard-code the row count.","<b>Find by content:</b> <code>//td[text()='Ravi']/following-sibling::td[2]</code> or <code>//tr[td[text()='Ravi']]//button</code>.","<b>Columns:</b> <code>//table[@id='t']//tr/td[3]</code> gives every value of column 3.","<b>Pagination:</b> loop until the Next button is disabled or absent."],"file":"WebTableDemo.java","path":"module13/WebTableDemo.java","code":"package com.seleniumlearning.module13;\n\nimport org.openqa.selenium.By;\nimport org.openqa.selenium.WebDriver;\nimport org.openqa.selenium.WebElement;\nimport org.openqa.selenium.chrome.ChromeDriver;\nimport io.github.bonigarcia.wdm.WebDriverManager;\nimport java.util.List;\n\npublic class WebTableDemo {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        WebDriverManager.chromedriver().setup();\n        WebDriver driver = new ChromeDriver();\n        driver.get(\"https://the-internet.herokuapp.com/tables\");\n\n        // --- Static Table Handling ---\n        WebElement table1 = driver.findElement(By.id(\"table1\"));\n        List<WebElement> rows = table1.findElements(By.cssSelector(\"tbody tr\"));\n        System.out.println(\"Total rows in table1: \" + rows.size());\n\n        // Print table header\n        List<WebElement> headers = table1.findElements(By.cssSelector(\"thead th\"));\n        System.out.print(\"Headers: \");\n        for (WebElement h : headers) System.out.print(h.getText() + \" | \");\n        System.out.println();\n\n        // Traverse each row and column\n        for (int i = 0; i < rows.size(); i++) {\n            List<WebElement> cols = rows.get(i).findElements(By.tagName(\"td\"));\n            System.out.print(\"Row \" + (i+1) + \": \");\n            for (WebElement col : cols) {\n                System.out.print(col.getText() + \" | \");\n            }\n            System.out.println();\n        }\n\n        // Get specific cell: 2nd row, 3rd column (Email)\n        String cellValue = driver.findElement(By.xpath(\"//table[@id='table1']/tbody/tr[2]/td[3]\")).getText();\n        System.out.println(\"Cell [2,3]: \" + cellValue);\n\n        // --- Dynamic Search in Table ---\n        String targetLastName = \"Doe\";\n        boolean found = false;\n        for (WebElement row : rows) {\n            if (row.getText().contains(targetLastName)) {\n                System.out.println(\"Found row with \" + targetLastName + \": \" + row.getText());\n                // Click action in that row, e.g., Edit link\n                WebElement editLink = row.findElement(By.linkText(\"edit\"));\n                System.out.println(\"Edit link href: \" + editLink.getAttribute(\"href\"));\n                found = true;\n                break;\n            }\n        }\n\n        // --- Calculation Example: Sum of Due column ($ symbol) ---\n        double totalDue = 0;\n        for (WebElement row : rows) {\n            List<WebElement> cols = row.findElements(By.tagName(\"td\"));\n            if (cols.size() >= 4) {\n                String dueText = cols.get(3).getText().replace(\"$\", \"\").trim();\n                totalDue += Double.parseDouble(dueText);\n            }\n        }\n        System.out.println(\"Total Due: $\" + totalDue);\n\n        driver.quit();\n    }\n}","steps":[{"title":"Table Structure Discovery","lines":"12-19","desc":"Find table by ID, then tbody tr for rows. Count rows. Separate thead th for headers — useful to find column index by header name instead of hardcoding index 3 for Email."},{"title":"Row/Column Iteration","lines":"21-31","desc":"Nested loops: outer rows, inner cols (td). Print or validate. For large tables, this is O(n*m). Use XPath for direct cell access when you know coordinates."},{"title":"Direct Cell Access","lines":"33-35","desc":"XPath //table[@id='table1']/tbody/tr[2]/td[3] gets specific cell. Faster than iterating if you know position. tr[2] is second row (1-based in XPath). Useful for assertions."},{"title":"Dynamic Search Pattern","lines":"37-50","desc":"Search for row containing text, then interact with action link in same row. row.findElement scopes search to that row only — crucial to get correct edit/delete button for that record."},{"title":"Data Calculation","lines":"52-62","desc":"Extract numeric column, parse (remove $), sum. Real-world: sum cart totals and assert equals displayed total. Handle NumberFormatException for empty cells."}],"snip":["List<WebElement> rows = driver.findElements(By.xpath(\"//table[@id='cart']/tbody/tr\"));\ndouble total = 0;\nfor (int i = 1; i <= rows.size(); i++) {\n  String name  = driver.findElement(By.xpath(\"//table[@id='cart']/tbody/tr[\"+i+\"]/td[1]\")).getText();\n  String price = driver.findElement(By.xpath(\"//table[@id='cart']/tbody/tr[\"+i+\"]/td[3]\")).getText();\n  total += Double.parseDouble(price.replace(\"$\",\"\").trim());\n}\nSystem.out.println(\"Total = \" + total);\n\n// action on a specific row\ndriver.findElement(By.xpath(\"//tr[td[text()='Ravi']]//button[text()='Edit']\")).click();"],"best":["Find column index by header text: loop headers, if header text equals 'Email' store index, then use that index for all rows — survives column reordering.","For pagination, while loop: search page, if not found and Next enabled, click Next, wait for staleness of table, repeat.","Use CSS tbody tr:nth-child(n) for nth row — faster than XPath when no text search needed."],"bad":["Using //table/tr — misses tbody that browser auto-inserts. Always //table/tbody/tr or //table//tr.","Hardcoding column index 3 for Due — breaks when new column added. Find by header name dynamically.","Not handling StaleElementReference after pagination click — table element becomes stale, need to re-find rows after navigation.","Real-world: sum the column and assert it equals the displayed total; handle <code>NumberFormatException</code> on empty cells.","Re-find elements inside the loop if the table refreshes, to avoid <code>StaleElementReferenceException</code>."],"sim":["[Locate] table#table1 -> FOUND","Total rows in table1: 4","Headers: Last Name | First Name | Email | Due | Web Site | Action | ","Row 1: Smith | John | jsmith@gmail.com | $50.00 | http://www.jsmith.com | edit delete | ","Row 2: Bach | Frank | fbach@yahoo.com | $51.00 | http://www.frank.com | edit delete | ","Row 3: Doe | Jason | jdoe@hotmail.com | $100.00 | http://www.jdoe.com | edit delete | ","Row 4: Conway | Tim | tconway@earthlink.net | $50.00 | http://www.timconway.com | edit delete | ","Cell [2,3]: fbach@yahoo.com","Found row with Doe: Doe Jason jdoe@hotmail.com $100.00 ...","Edit link href: #edit","Total Due: $251.0"]}];
